[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2607.07022, 'Coordinate-wise Elephant Random Walk'] Define a martingale difference sequence $\eta_{r+1}^{(i)} := \1_{\{Y_{r+1}^{(i)}=1\}}-\E[\1_{\{Y_{r+1}^{(i)}=1\}}\mid\G_r^{(i)}]$, $r \ge 0 $ with $\E[\eta^{(i)}_{r+1}\mid \G ^{(i)}_r]=0$ and $\E[(\eta ^{(i)}_{r+1})^2\mid \G^{(i)}_r] \leq {1}/{4}$.
    $(x_r^{(i)})_{r\ge 0}$ in \eqref{eq:xri} satisfies 
    \begin{equation} 
        x^{(i)}_{r+1}-\frac{1}{2}=\left(1-\frac{2(1-p_i)}{r+2}\right)\left(x^{(i)}_r-\frac{1}{2} \right)+\frac{\eta^{(i)}_{r+1}}{r+2}, \quad r \ge 0 . 
    \end{equation}

