[Lem 20 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $\mathcal{S}^{(y,n)}$ be as in (\ref{shannonsum}). Then,
\begin{align}
\mathcal{S}^{(y,n)} =\left(\frac{y}{2}\right)^n\mathcal{S}^{(n)}  + y^n\left(\log(2) - \log(y)\right)n, \notag
\end{align}
for every $n\geq 2$ and any finite $y\in\R_+\setminus\{0\}$.

