[Lemma definition:twop-headc of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] The two point Palm probability distribution of ${\mathcal H }_c$ is

\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}_{{\mathcal H }_c}^{(t, h,C),(t', h',C')}(\, \cdot\, ):=\mathbb{P}\left({\mathcal H }_c^{(t, h,C), (t', h',C')}\in \cdot\, \right),{\nonumber}

\end{equation}

with ${\mathcal H }_c^{(t, h,C), (t', h',C')}:={\mathcal H }_c+ \delta_{(t, h,C)}+\delta_{(t', h',C')}$
and ${\mathcal H }_c$ the stationary version of the head point process.
Here $C$ and $C'$ are the radial birds with head point at $(t,h)$ and $(t',h')$, respectively. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

