[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.10266, 'A singular SDE driven by additive fractional Brownian motion with Hurst parameter $H<\frac'] There exists a positive constants $C=C(T, H,X_0, a)$ such that for all $\vare>0$ and all $t\in[0,T]$ we have
\begin{equation}
X_t^\vare\leq C+2\si\sup\limits_{s\in[0,T]}|B^H_s|.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 31 (Integral Asymptotics 3) of arXiv:2608.18834, 'The Parabolic Anderson Model's Total Mass at Small Times: Geometry, Fluctuations, and Reno'] Suppose that $\rho<0$, which, under Assumption \ref{Assumption}, implies that $H_0<1$. 
There is a bounded continuous function $\msf z_0:(0,\infty)\to\mbb R$
such that
for every $\th>0$, one has
\begin{align}

\msf J(\th)=8\Ga(-\rho)\left(\int_0^{\pi/2}\frac{(\cos\theta)^{-(2H_0-1)}(\sin\theta)^{d-H}}{\big(\cos\theta+\sin\theta\big)^{-\rho}}\d\theta\right)\th^{\rho}+\msf z_0(\th).
\end{align}
Moreover, one has
\begin{align}

\lim_{\th\to0}\msf z_0(\th)=
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle \frac{4\Ga(H_0)\Ga(1-H_0)\Gamma(d-H)}{\Ga(2H_0-1)(1+\rho)\rho}&H_0>1/2,\\
0&H_0=1/2.
\end{cases}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

