body:
[Lem eq:PilingD of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] Let $A$ be a valid DDM\xspace process on ${\cal C}_n$. If the masses $(m_0,\cdots,m_{k-1})$ are non-negative multiple of $1/n$ and satisfy $W(m[k])<1$, then, the discrete piling propensity is
	\begin{equation}
	Q^{(n)}(m[k])=\mathbb{P}({\bf N}_k^{(n)}=1) =
	\left(W(m[k])+\frac1n\right)^{k-1}.
	\end{equation} Moreover, for any $\ell\in{\cal C}_n$, by letting $A_j$ be the starting point of the block $j$, we have,
	\begin{equation}\mathbb{P}\left({\bf N}_k^{(n)}=1,A_0=\ell\right)= Q^{(n)}(m[k])/ n.  \end{equation}

