body:
[Theorem 18 (Independent-row comparison) of arXiv:2607.20329, '2607.20329'] Let $A\in\mathbb K^{n\times n}$ have independent rows
		$R_1,\ldots,R_n$.  Suppose that, for some $\sigma_1,\ldots,\sigma_n>0$,
		\begin{equation}
			\E R_i^*R_i=\sigma_i^2I_n,
			\qquad
			\gamma_{1,\beta}
			\le_{\mathrm{Lt}}
			\frac{|R_ic|^2}{\sigma_i^2\|c\|_2^2}
			\quad(c\in\mathbb K^n\setminus\{0\}).
		\end{equation}
		Then
		\begin{equation}
			\Delta_n^{\mathbb K}
			\le_{\mathrm{Lt}}X_n^{\mathbb K}
			\le_{\mathrm{Lt}}
			\frac{|\per_{\mathbb K}A|^2}
			{n!\prod_{i=1}^n\sigma_i^2}.
		\end{equation}
		Consequently, for every $\varepsilon>0$,
		\begin{equation}
			\Pp\left(
			|\per_{\mathbb K}A|
			\le\varepsilon\sqrt{n!}\prod_{i=1}^n\sigma_i
			\right)
			\le
			\min\left\{1,
			\left(\frac{2\pi e}{\beta}\right)^{\beta/2}
			\kappa_{n,\beta}\varepsilon^\beta
			\right\}.
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

