[Proposition prop:lbm-response-realization of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For every $\mu\in\mathcal M_{\rm LBM}$ and every $u,v$ in a common
positive eigenspace of $A_\mu$,
\begin{equation}
 \Theta_\mu(u,v)=uv\,\mu\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D).

\end{equation}
The map $U_\mu=U_D$ in (equation eq:lbm-response-space of the paper) is linear and
injective, and
\begin{equation}
 \inner{U_\mu\sigma}{f}_{H}
 =\int_Df\,d\sigma,
 \qquad
 \sigma\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D),\quad f\in C_c^\infty(D).

\end{equation}
Thus the LBM response is faithfully potential-realizable in the sense of
Definition~(def:response-realization of the paper).

[Lemma 6 (Weighted vector Bochner identity) of arXiv:2607.10769, '\fontsize{14}{17}\selectfont\bfseries Sharp Poincar\'e interpolation along Wasserstein geo'] For every $X\in C_c^\infty(\R^n;\R^n)$,
\begin{equation}
 \int(\diver_\mu X)^2\,\d\mu
 =
 \int\left\{\tr((DX)^2)+\Hess{V}[X,X]\right\}\,\d\mu.
\end{equation}

