[Lemma 93 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $Y : [0,T] \to D(A)$ be measurable and bounded. We define the path $Z : [0,T] \to W$ as
\begin{align*}
Z_t := \int_0^t S_{t-s} Y_s \, ds, \quad t \in [0,T].
\end{align*}
Then we have
\begin{align*}
|Z_{s,t}| \leq (1+T) M e^{\omega T} \| Y \|_{\infty} |t-s| \quad \text{for all $s,t \in [0,T]$.}
\end{align*}

