[Lemma 56 of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] Let $\eps_f>0$, let $f\colon (0,\eps_f)\to \NN_{\ge2}$, and let $s>0$.
    If \begin{equation*}
       \liminf_{\eps\downarrow 0} \frac{\log_2\log_2 f(\eps)}{\log_2\big(\frac{1}{\eps}\big)} \ge s,
    \end{equation*}
    then for every $t\in (0,s)$ there exists $\eps_0\in (0,\eps_f)$
    such that $f(\eps) \ge 2^{\eps^{-t}}$ for all $\eps\in (0,\eps_0)$.

