[Theorem thm:kwise of arXiv:2607.22991, 'Mixing times and spectra of non-equilibrium symmetric exclusion processes on general graph'] For any SEP with arbitrary heat baths, there is an algorithm running in time $n^{O(k)}(\log \tau_{\rm hit} +\log\log\varepsilon^{-1})$ that
computes the joint occupation distribution of any $k$ vertices in~$G$ within variation distance~$\varepsilon$, 
for any $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

