[Theorem 12 (Minimax lower bound) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] If $\widehat p_t(\cdot|X_t,\cG_{t-1})$ ranges over all sequential predictive densities that may use the revealed context $X_t$ and past history $\cG_{t-1}$, then
    \begin{align*}
    \inf_{(\widehat p_t)}\sup_{\theta^\star\in\ThetaSob}
    \E\sbr{ \sum_{t=1}^T\log\frac{p_{\star,X_t}(Y_t)}{\widehat p_t(Y_t| X_t,\cG_{t-1})}}
    \gtrsim T^{1/\zeta}.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 1 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $\Omega$ satisfying 
\begin{equation} 
\forall x,y \in \bb Z, \; \forall \eta \in \Omega, \quad \nu(\eta^{x,y})=\nu(\eta).
\end{equation}
Then, under condition \eqref{pairbal}, the measure $\nu$ is invariant with respect to the dynamics given by $\mcb L^n$.

