[Lemma lem:IBJ-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] Let $H = \ell^2(\mathbb{Z})$.  The seed functions
$\psi_{t,a,n}$ and $\phi_{t,a,n}$ defined in
\S(sec:IBJ-kernel-reform of the paper) satisfy the linear
problem (equation eq:Linear-Psi-3 of the paper) and the adjoint
linear problem (equation eq:Linear-Phi-Prob of the paper) on
$\mathcal{V}$ with edge weights
$(c_k, \lambda_k)$.  Explicitly:
\begin{align}
\psi_{t,a,n+1}
&= q_{n+1}\psi_{t,a+1,n}
   - \psi_{t,a,n},
 \\
\psi_{t+1,a+1,n}
&= \psi_{t,a+1,n}
   + p_{t+1}\psi_{t,a,n},

\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\phi_{t,a+1,n}
&= q_{n+1}\phi_{t,a,n+1}
   - \phi_{t,a+1,n+1},
 \\
\phi_{t,a+1,n}
&= \phi_{t+1,a+1,n}
   + p_{t+1}\phi_{t+1,a+2,n}.

\end{align}

