[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2605.31344, 'Subcritical sharpness for real-valued spin models'] For any $\beta \geq 0$, there exists a probability measure $\Psi_{\beta}^{1}$ on $(\mathbb{R}^+)^{V} \times \{0, 1\}^{E}$ such that for any $\lambda \in \mathbb{R}$ and any $\sfb \in \mathbb{R}^{V}$ with $\eta^{+}_x \leq \sfb_x \leq e^{\lambda d_G(o, x)}$ for all $x \in V$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \Psi_{\Lambda, \beta}^{(w, \sfb)} \rightarrow \Psi_{\beta}^{1}
        \text{ as } \Lambda \nearrow V.
    \end{equation*}

