[Lem lem-hm-linear of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] For each $x\in \mathcal V\mathcal G$, the harmonic measure $\operatorname{hm}_{\mathcal A}^x$ is a probability measure on $\mathcal A$. 
Moreover, for each $\phi : \mathcal A \to\mathbbm R$, the energy-minimizing discrete harmonic function $h^\phi$ satisfies
\begin{equation}   
h^\phi(x)= \sum_{y\in \mathcal A} \phi(y) \operatorname{hm}_{\mathcal A}^x(y) .
\end{equation}

