[Lemma lem: Conjugation of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] There exist functions $\xi(x), (\mu_j(x),\nu_j(x))_{1\le j\le 4}$, holomorphic in a neighborhood of the $x=0$,
dependent on $(d,\ell,r)$,  such that the change of variables
\begin{equation}

\left|\begin{array}{l}
\tilde{\Psi}(x)=M(x)\Phi(x), \ \ M(x)=e^{-\int_0^x \xi(y)dy}\\
\Theta(x)=\frac{\Phi(x)}{x}
\end{array}\right.
\end{equation} 
maps (equation eq: Formal Limit Equation of the paper) to 
\begin{equation}

x^2\Theta'+[a_\infty+(\nu_\infty+3)x]\Theta=\mu_0+x\left[x\sum_{j=1}^4\mu_j\Theta^j+x^2(x\Theta')\sum_{j=1}^{4}\nu_j\Theta^j\right].
\end{equation}

