[Thm th.Ress of arXiv:2411.13099, 'Long time behavior of killed Feynman-Kac semigroups with singular Schr{ö}dinger potentials'] Assume  {\rm \textbf{[c1]}} or {\rm \textbf{[c2]}} and assume also    {\rm \textbf{[S1]}} or {\rm \textbf{[S2]}}.   
Moreover, assume  that there exist   constants ${\mathfrak m_0},{\mathfrak r_0},{\mathfrak b_0}>0$,  a compact subset $\mathscr K_0$ of $\mathscr R^d_0=\mathscr R^d\setminus \{0\}$, and   a $\mathcal C^2$  function $\mathbf W_\star:\mathscr R^d  \to [1,+\infty)$  such  that 

\begin{equation}
\frac{\mathscr L^{oL}  \mathbf W_\star }{\mathbf W_\star }-   \mathbf V_{\mathbf S}\le -{\mathfrak r_0} \mathbf 1_{\mathscr R^d_0\setminus \mathscr K_0} + {\mathfrak b_0}\mathbf 1_{\mathscr K_0} \text{ on } \mathscr R^d_0, 
\end{equation}
and for some $p>1$, 
\begin{equation}
( \mathscr L^{oL} - \mathbf V_{\mathbf S})\mathbf W_\star^p\le {\mathfrak m_0} \mathbf W_\star^p \text{ on } \mathscr R^d_0.
\end{equation}

Then, for all $t\ge 0$, $T^{oL}_t$ is a bounded operator on $b\mathcal B_{\mathbf W_\star}(\mathscr R^d_0)$. In addition (see (equation eq.betaw of the paper) and (equation eq.Ttt of the paper) for the definitions of $\beta_w$ and $T^{oL}_{t,\mathbf W_\star}$), for $t>0$, 
$$\beta_w(T^{oL}_{t,\mathbf W_\star}|_{b\mathcal B (\mathscr R^d_0)})\le e^{-{\mathfrak r_0}t}\,  \text{ and  } \, \mathsf r_{ess}(T^{oL}_t|_{b\mathcal B_{\mathbf W_\star}(\mathscr R^d_0)})\le e^{-{\mathfrak r_0}t}.$$

[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$ and $v\neq w\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ with $|v-w|\ge 10d$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{K}_{\{v,w\}}(v,w)\asymp |v-w|^{2-d}.
	\end{equation}

