body:
[Theorem thm:flow-CD of arXiv:2603.14906, 'Four Levels of Thermodynamic Convergence of Singularly Perturbed Markov Semigroups'] Assume that there exist $\varepsilon_0>0$ and $\rho\in\mathbb{R}$ such that for every $0<\varepsilon\le\varepsilon_0$, every
$z_1,z_2\in E$, and every $t\ge0$, the synchronously coupled solutions
$Z_t^{1,\varepsilon},Z_t^{2,\varepsilon}$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E\Big[
    (Z_t^{1,\varepsilon}-Z_t^{2,\varepsilon})^\top
    \big(A^\varepsilon(Z_t^{1,\varepsilon})\big)^{-1}
    (Z_t^{1,\varepsilon}-Z_t^{2,\varepsilon})
  \Big]
  \;\le\;
  e^{2\rho t}\,
  (z_1-z_2)^\top \big(A^\varepsilon(z_1)\big)^{-1}(z_1-z_2).
\end{equation}
Then, for every $0<\varepsilon\le\varepsilon_0$, the gradient commutation estimate
\begin{equation}
  \Gamma^\varepsilon(P_t^\varepsilon f)(z)
  \;\le\;
  e^{2\rho t}\,\big(P_t^\varepsilon\Gamma^\varepsilon(f)\big)(z),
  \qquad t\ge0,\ z\in E,\ f\in \mathcal{M}.
\end{equation}
holds. In particular, $P_t^\varepsilon$ satisfies the curvature--dimension condition $CD(-\rho,\infty)$ uniformly in
$\varepsilon\in(0,\varepsilon_0]$.

