[Lemma lem:circle-cylinder-to-local-dimension-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Let \(\nu\) be a finite Borel measure on \(\mathbb S^1\). Suppose that, for some \(\beta\ge0\), there is a constant \(C<\infty\) such that
\begin{equation*}
\nu(\mathcal I_v)\le C2^{-\beta \lvert v \rvert}
\qquad(v\in\mathcal T).
\end{equation*}
Then
\begin{equation*}
\liminf_{r\downarrow0}
\frac{\log_2\nu(B(x,r))}{\log_2 r}\ge\beta
\qquad
(x\in\operatorname{spt}\nu).
\end{equation*}

