[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] The BPHZ model $(\tilde\Pi^{\eps, \delta}, \tilde \Gamma^{\eps, \delta})$ on $\tilde{\mfT}$ associated to the noise assignment 
	given in Definition~\ref{def:tcT_noise_ass}
	is bounded in $L^p(d\mathbb{P}; \mathcal{M})$ uniformly in $0 < \delta < \eps < 1$ for all $p \in [1, \infty)$ where $\mathcal{M}$ is the space of models on $\tilde{\mfT}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:lbstrthm1 of arXiv:2607.26551, 'An RDT based confirmation of Lehner's formula for Kronecker-Gaussian matrices'] For large $n\in{\mathbb N}$ and fixed $k,l\in{\mathbb N}$, let $G_{i}\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times n}$, $G_{i}^{(1,1)},G_{i}^{(1,2)},G_{i}^{(1)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k\times n},i=1,\dots,l$ be independent  standard normal matrices. Let $R$, $A_i$,  and $F_i$ be as in  Theorem (thm:thm1 of the paper). Also, let $U_iD_iU_i^T=F_i$ be the eigen-decomposition of $F_i$ ($U_i$ is unitary and $D$ is diagonal). For  $t\in(0,1)$ and $Q\in{\mathcal Q}$, let $D^{(2)}(t)$   be as in ((eq:lbstr3a1 of the paper)) and  ((eq:lbstr3 of the paper)). Set $G_i^{(1,3)} = Q G_i^{(1,1)} + \sqrt{I-Q^TQ}G_i^{(1,2)}$, 
 \begin{eqnarray}

 \bar{\zeta}_i^{(1,1)}(X^{(1)}) & = & \mbox{Tr}(G_i^{(1,1)}  X^{(1)} F_i) 
 \nonumber \\
 \bar{\zeta}_i^{(1,3)}(X^{(2)}) & = & \mbox{Tr}(G_i^{(1,3)}  X^{(2)} F_i) , 
 \end{eqnarray} 
and
\begin{equation}

{\mathcal G}_{D_u} (X^{(1)},X^{(2)}) =    
\sqrt{2} \left (
\sqrt{t} \sum_{i=1}^{l}    \bar{\zeta}_i^{(1,1)}(X^{(1)})
+\sqrt{t} \sum_{i=1}^{l}    \bar{\zeta}_i^{(1,3)}(X^{(2)})
+\sqrt{1-t} \sum_{j=1}^{2}  \sum_{i=1}^{l}   \zeta_i^{(2)}(X^{(j)})
\right ) .
\end{equation} 
Let
\begin{equation}

L^{(2)}(t)=  \max_{(X^{(1)},X^{(2)})\in\bar{{\mathcal X}}}  
 {\mathcal G}_{D_u} (X^{(1)},X^{(2)}) .
\end{equation} 
 One then has  
\begin{eqnarray}

\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} {\mathbb E} D^{(2)}(t) 
\leq 
\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} {\mathbb E} L^{(2)}(t) .
\end{eqnarray}

