[Thm 5 of arXiv:2605.05430, 'Dirichlet problems and exit distributions for the telegraph process and its planar extensi'] For $j=1,3$, the Fourier transforms $\widetilde{u}_j(\alpha,y\mathord{;}z)$ read
\begin{equation}\widetilde{u}_1(\alpha,y\mathord{;}z)=\frac{2\lambda^2\sinh\left(\frac{\lvert\alpha\lvert\lambda(L-y)}{\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}}\right)e^{i\alpha z}}{\big(\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}+\lvert\alpha\lvert c\big)^2\;e^{\frac{\lvert\alpha\lvert\,\lambda\,L}{\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}}}-\big(\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}-\lvert\alpha\lvert c\big)^2\;e^{-\frac{\lvert\alpha\lvert\,\lambda\,L}{\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}}}}\end{equation}
and
\begin{align}\widetilde{u}_3(\alpha,&\,y\mathord{;}z)=\nonumber\\
&e^{i\alpha z}\,\frac{\big(\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}+\lvert\alpha\lvert c\big)^2\;e^{\frac{\lvert\alpha\lvert\,\lambda\,(L-y)}{\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}}}-\big(\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}-\lvert\alpha\lvert c\big)^2\;e^{-\frac{\lvert\alpha\lvert\,\lambda\,(L-y)}{\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}}}}{\big(\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}+\lvert\alpha\lvert c\big)^2\;e^{\frac{\lvert\alpha\lvert\,\lambda\,L}{\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}}}-\big(\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}-\lvert\alpha\lvert c\big)^2\;e^{-\frac{\lvert\alpha\lvert\,\lambda\,L}{\sqrt{\lambda^2+\alpha^2c^2}}}}.\end{align}
For $j=0,2$, the Fourier transforms $\widetilde{u}_0(\alpha,y\mathord{;}z)$ and $\widetilde{u}_2(\alpha,y\mathord{;}z)$ follow immediately by the identities in equation (\ref{algebrain}).

