[Lemma 69 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $K\in \N$ and $0 < t_1 < t_2 < \dots < t_K$. Then for any $\varepsilon'>0$ and initial data $\hfixp_0 \in \UCp$, we have
\begin{equation}
     \bigg\lVert \Big(\hfixpa(\hfixp_0;\cdot,t_\ell)\Big)_{\ell \in \lbr K \rbr} -  \Big(\hfixp(\hfixp_0;\cdot,t_\ell)\Big)_{\ell \in \lbr K \rbr}  \bigg\rVert_{\textup{TV}} \leq \varepsilon^{\prime} 
\end{equation} for all $n=n(\delta,\varepsilon^{\prime})$ large enough.

