[Theorem th:ErdosTaylor of arXiv:2509.16694, 'A central limit theorem for two-dimensional directed polymers with critical spatial correl'] As $N\to\infty$, the following convergence in distribution holds
\begin{equation} 
    \frac{(a+2)^2\, 2^{a}}{\left(\log N\right)^{a+2}}  \sum_{n=1}^N h(S_{2n}) \stackrel{{ (d)}}{\longrightarrow} \tau_{0,1}^{\alpha}\,,
\end{equation}
where $\tau_{0,1}^{\alpha}$ is the first hitting time of $1$ of a Bessel process of order $2\alpha+2$ started at $0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

