[Lemma nonregu0 of arXiv:2411.15881, 'Stable Approximation for Call Function Via Stein's method'] For any $M>2$ and let $f_{g_{M}}$ be the solution to equation (equation stablestein of the paper), then for any $y\in\left(-\infty,\infty\right)$, we have
\begin{align*}
\|f''_{g_{M}}(y)\|_{\infty}
\leq\frac{\eta_{4,\alpha}}{M^{\frac{\alpha^{2}-1}{\alpha^{2}+2\alpha-1}}},
\end{align*}
where $\eta_{4,\alpha}$ is defined by (equation 6 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:atoms of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] The limiting law has no atoms in $(0,\infty)$, and
\begin{equation}
  \mu_{c,\lambda,v}(\{0\})=\left(1-\frac1c\right)_+.

\end{equation}

[Proposition 15 (Malliavin derivative estimates) of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] Let $X$ be the unique strong solution to \eqref{eq: averaged dynamics 1}. Then $X \in \bbL^{1, 2}_T$ and there exists $C \in (0, \infty)$ depending only on $(A, \beta, T, C_{\textup{Lip}})$ such that for arbitrary $i=1,\dots,N$, 
\begin{equation*}
     \bbE\big[|D_u^i X_t|^2\big]+\int_0^t \int_0^t \bbE\big[|D_r^i X_s|^2\big]\,dr\,ds\leq C, \quad 0 \leq u \leq t \leq T.
\end{equation*}
Moreover with $Q$ as in \eqref{eq: averaged dynamics 1}, we have
\begin{equation*}
    \bbE\big[\|D^i_s Q_t\|^2_{\op}\big] \leq CN^{-1}, \quad i = 1, \ldots, N, \quad 0 \leq s \leq t \leq T.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:inverse of arXiv:2411.15954, 'A gradient model for the Bernstein polynomial basis'] For each $n,L\in\mathbb{N}$ with $L>n$, it holds that
    \begin{align}
    \mathbf{p}_{\ell;L}(\eta)
    &=\sum_{n=\ell}^L
    \frac{\binom{n}{\ell}}{\binom{L}{\ell}}
    \mathbf{b}_{n,L}.
\end{align}

