{"artifact_digest":"sha256:aa02aba234a3d50e1dc6d3a8d9ef7db5ad83113cb7522b43387923590caa6bbf","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/aa/aa02aba234a3d50e1dc6d3a8d9ef7db5ad83113cb7522b43387923590caa6bbf.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:7129fdf1ad9dc2c59ca14c76aa51540e3de01256c0a8e0934b90ea191dabf9a8","bundle_entry_key":"2602-21315-lemma-55-bottleneck-geo-bound","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_066","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_066.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2602-21315-lemma-55-bottleneck-geo-bound","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let $i^+$ be the smallest integer satisfying (iii) in the definition of bottleneck (Definition~(def:bottleneck of the paper)).
We divide the geometric variables into three classes. Let
    \begin{align*}
        \Sigma_1 &= \{j \in \{0,\ldots,i-1\} \colon W_j \le i^+/\log i^+\},\\
        \Sigma_2 &= \{j \in \{0,\ldots,i-1\} \colon i^+/\log i^+ < W_j \le (i^+)^{\chi}\},\\
\Sigma_3 &= \{j \in \{0,\ldots,i-1\} \colon W_j > (i^+)^{\chi}\},
    \end{align*}
where $\chi = 1000$ from Definition~(def:constants of the paper). 
