[Lemma beta-in of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] For all non-negative measurable functions $f$ on $(\Omega,{\mathcal F })$ we have:
\begin{enumerate}[(i).]
    \item  For all $l\in [n]$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}_{{\mathcal V }_l}^0 [f ({\mathcal H })]=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathcal R }_l}^0 \left[f (\theta_{\beta_l(0)}({\mathcal H }))\right], 

\end{equation}
where $\beta_l$ is the bijection between the point processes ${\mathcal V }_l$ and ${\mathcal R }_l$.
\item  For all $l\neq r\in [n], k= 1,2$,

\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}_{{\mathcal V }^{(k)}_{l,r}}^0 [f ({\mathcal H })]=\mathbb{E}_{{\mathcal R }^{(k)}_{l,r}}^0 \left[f (\theta_{\beta^{(k)}_{l,r}(0)}({\mathcal H }))\right], 

\end{equation}
where $\beta^{(k)}_{l,r}$ is the bijection between the point processes ${\mathcal V }_{l,r}^{(k)}$ and ${\mathcal R }_{l,r}^{(k)}$, of type $\binom{k}{l,r}$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

