[Definition def:symmetric:positive of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] Let \( R : X^* \to X \) be an operator.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item \( R \) is \emph{symmetric} if \( \langle Rf, g \rangle = \langle Rg, f \rangle \) for all \( f,g \in X^* \) .
        \item \( R \) is \emph{positive} if \( \langle Rf, f \rangle \geq 0 \) for all \( f \in X^* \).
    \end{enumerate}

