[Theorem th:main_result of arXiv:2506.17168, '{\bf Scaling limits for sample autocovariance operators of Hilbert space-valued linear pro'] Let $\{X_{n}\}_{n \in \mathbb Z}$ be an $\mathbb{H}$-valued linear process (equation eq:linear_process of the paper), (equation eq:linear_process2 of the paper), and consider its autocovariance operators $(\widehat \Gamma_{N,h}, h = 0,\dots,H)$ given in (equation eq:SampleAutoShort of the paper). Suppose (equation eq:second_regime of the paper),
\begin{equation} 
  \operatorname{E} \|U \varepsilon_{0} \|^4_{L^4(\mathbb{Y})} < \infty 
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation} 
\int_{\mathbb{Y}} \frac{\operatorname{E} (U \varepsilon_0)^2(r)}{(1-2d(r))(2d(r) - 1/2)}	\mu(dr)  < \infty.
\end{equation}
Then,
\begin{equation*}
\Delta^U_{N} \begin{pmatrix}
    \widehat{\Gamma}_{N,0}-\Gamma_{0} \\
    \vdots \\
    \widehat{\Gamma}_{N,H}-\Gamma_{H}
\end{pmatrix}
\overset{\operatorname{d}}{\to}
\begin{pmatrix}
\mathfrak{Z}_U \\
\vdots \\
\mathfrak{Z}_U
\end{pmatrix}
\in (\mathbb{H} \otimes \mathbb{H})^{\times (H+1)},
\end{equation*}		
where $\Delta^U_N$ is defined in (equation eq:scaling:Delta of the paper) and $\mathfrak{Z}_U$ is defined in (equation equality_f^(u,l)_t,(m,s) of the paper)--(equation eq:Ztilde of the paper) below. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

