[Proposition 6 (Orthogonality of the $H_n(X)$) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For any $n, m\in\N_0$, one has 
\begin{equation}

 \expec{H_n(X)H_m(X)} =
 n!\delta_{nm} = 
 \begin{cases}
  n! & \text{if $n = m$\;,} \\
  0 & \text{otherwise\;.}
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}

