[Lemma 10 (Four-dimensional three-form algebra) of arXiv:2608.30638, 'On compact steady pluriclosed soliton surfaces'] Let $(V,g)$ be an oriented real four dimensional vector space endowed with a positive definite metric $g$. If $\theta$ is a one-form and
$H=-*\theta$, then for every vector $X\in V$,
\begin{equation}
 \iota_XH=-*(\theta\wedge X^\flat),
 \qquad
 H^2=2\bigl(|\theta|^2g-\theta\otimes\theta\bigr).
\end{equation}
Thus $H^2\geq0$ and, wherever $H\ne0$,
\begin{equation}
 \ker H^2=\{X:\iota_XH=0\}=\mathbb R\theta^\sharp.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 6.2 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For every $\ka>0$, there exists some $\th_\ka>0$ such that
for every $m=1,2$ and $t\in(0,\th_\ka)$ the following sequences of random variables are uniformly integrable:
\[\big\{\msf T_{\ka,\eps}(t)^m\mr e^{-mt\msf c_{\ka,\eps}}:\eps>0\big\}
\qquad\text{and}\qquad
\big\{\msf M_{\ka,\eps}(t)^m\mr e^{-mt\msf c_{\ka,\eps}}:\eps>0\big\}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

