[Theorem thm21 of arXiv:2605.16160, 'Revisiting Toeplitz and Hankel random matrices via $*$-convergence of circulant-type matri'] Let $C_n$ be a random circulant matrix with independent entries that satisfy Assumption I. 
     Let $D_n(\theta)$ be as in ((eqn:defndn of the paper)). Then there exists a $*$-probability space $(\mathcal{A}, \varphi)$ so that for any  monomial $Q$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\varphi_n(Q(n^{-1/2}C_n,D_n(\theta))){\rightarrow} \varphi(Q(N,d(\theta)))\ \text{as}\ n\rightarrow\infty,
    \end{equation*}
    where the distributions ($*$-moments) of $N$ and $d(\theta)$ are respectively those of a standard complex Gaussian variable and as in Lemma (lemma1 of the paper) respectively. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 13 of arXiv:2607.21759, 'Marchenko--Pastur law for tensor powers of exchangeable unconditional vectors'] Let $d = o(\sqrt n)$. Assume $(X_1,\dotsc,X_n) \sim \Inv_k(R)$ for some fixed $k \in (0,\infty]$. Define \[Q(k) = \begin{cases} \frac{\Gamma(3/k)}{\Gamma(1/k)} \cdot \bigl(\frac{n}{k}\bigr)^{-2/k} & \text{if }k<\infty, \\ 1/3 & \text{if }k=\infty. \end{cases}\] Then as $n \to \infty$, if \begin{enumerate}
    \item ${Q(k)}^d \cdot \E(R^{2d})\to 1$, and 
    \item ${Q(k)}^{2d} \cdot \bigl[\E(R^{4d}) - \bigl(\E R^{2d}\bigr)^2\bigr] \to 0$, 
\end{enumerate}
then the three conditions in \cref{thm:main} are satisfied, and we have $\ESD(K_{\PrincipalT}) \wkconv \mu_{\MP(c)}$ with probability $1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

