[Lemma lem: BlockDiagonalDecomposition of arXiv:2603.26932, 'On the satisfaction frequency of spectral characterization conditions'] Consider a matrix $\bM \in \sO^{n\times n}$ that is symmetric, $\bM = \bM^{\T}$. 
    Then, for every $k\leq n$, it holds that $\rank_q(\bM) = n-k$ if and only if there exists invertible $\bG \in \operatorname{GL}_n(\sO)$ such that 
    \begin{align}
        \bG^{\T}\bM\bG = \begin{pmatrix}
            \bQ & 0 \\ 
            0 & \bK
        \end{pmatrix}
    \end{align}
    for some symmetric $\bK \in \mathfrak{m}^{k\times k}$ and invertible symmetric $\bQ \in \operatorname{GL}_{n-k}(\sO)$.

