[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Suppose the edge weights are such that $c^{-1} \leq \weight(e) \leq c$ for some $c \geq 1$. Then there exist constants $c_1, c_2, c_3, c_4 > 0$ such that the lazy random walk transition kernel $q_n(\cdot, \cdot)$ on the weighted graph $(\mathbb{L}^d, \weight)$ satisfies
    \begin{equation} 
        c_1 \frac{1}{n^{d/2}} e^{- c_2 \frac{\Vert x - y \Vert^2}{n}} \leq q_n(x,y) \leq c_3 \frac{1}{n^{d/2}} e^{- c_4 \frac{\Vert x - y \Vert^2}{n}},
    \end{equation}
    for any $x, y \in \Z^d$ and $n \geq \Vert x - y\Vert$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

