[Lemma lem:permutation-nilpotent of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let ${\mathbf Y}_n^{(0)}$ be a one-hot matrix. Then, up to conjugation by permutation matrices, ${\mathbf Y}_n^{(0)}$ admits the decomposition in upper triangular form  
    \begin{equation*}
        {\mathbf Y}_n^{(0)} = \begin{pmatrix}
            N & * \\
            0 & P
        \end{pmatrix}\,,
    \end{equation*}
    where $N$ is a nilpotent matrix and $P \in \{-1, 1 \} \wr \mathfrak{S}_r$ is a signed permutation matrix  of size $1 \leqslant r \leqslant n$.

