[Definition of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] We say $\mathfrak{F} = (W, \leq, \sqsubset)$ is a \emph{fusion frame (f-frame)}\footnote{
    We use ``fusion'' to remain neutral between the IML and CML traditions.
  } if $W$ is a non-empty set, $\leq$ is a preorder on $W$, and $\sqsubset$ is a binary relation on $W$.
  We say $\mathfrak{M} = (\mathfrak{F}, V)$ is a \emph{fusion model (f-model)} if $\mathfrak{F}$ is an f-frame and $V: \mathord{\mathrm{PropVar}} \to \mathcal{P}(W)$,
  where each $V(p)$ is upward closed with respect to $\leq$.
  Such $\mathfrak{M}$ is said to be \emph{based on} $\mathfrak{F}$.

[Proposition prop: stochastic boundary v2 of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] For every $i\in\{1,2,3\}$, $\alpha \in (\max(0,\frac{i-2}{2}),i/2]$, every $\delta > 0$ sufficiently small, and for every $p\in[1,\infty)$ there exists $C_p>0$ such that  and 
\begin{equation} 
\sup_T \mathbb E\Big[ \Big( \sup_{\tau \in [-1,1]}|\tau|^{\alpha}\| \llbracket (\overline H  W^0_T) ^i \rrbracket (\tau,\cdot)\|_{\mathcal C^{-i/2+\alpha-\delta}_z} \Big)^p \Big] \leq C_p. 
\end{equation}
Furthermore,  there exists a random variable $\llbracket (\overline H W^0_\infty)^i\rrbracket \in L^\infty(|\tau|^{\alpha},\mathcal C^{-i/2+\alpha-\delta}_z)$ -- where this weighted space is defined with the norm appearing inside the expectation (equation eq:stoch-weighted-linfty of the paper) --  such that for every sequence $(T_n) : T_n\rightarrow \infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
\llbracket (\overline H W^0_{T_n})^i\rrbracket\rightarrow \llbracket (\overline H W^0_\infty)^i\rrbracket \, \text{ in }L^\infty(|\tau|^{\alpha},\mathcal C^{-i/2+\alpha-\delta}_z).
\end{equation}
The estimates also hold with $\overline H$ replaced by $H$, and the single harmonic extension replaced by the double harmonic extension. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2606.22656, 'Fluctuations of Point Vortex Ensembles\\ at Small Negative Inverse Temperature'] For every $0<\beta<\beta_0$,
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{N\to\infty}Z_N^\pm(\beta)
    =\dettwo(I-\beta G)^{-1/2}.
\end{equation*}
The law of $\omega_N^\pm$ under the canonical ensemble distribution of positions with partition function $Z_N^\pm(\beta)$, $0<\beta<\min(\beta_0,\beta_\star)$, weakly converges to $\mu_\beta$.

