body:
[Proposition prop:locprob of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Under the conditions of Theorem (thm:lattice of the paper) one has for $z=x/\sigma$
\begin{align*}
    \mathbf P(S_n = x) 
=
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 n}}
    \sum_{j=0}^{2r+2}
        \frac{P_j^{(0)}(z)}{n^{j+1/2}}     
+
    w_n(x)
    , \quad n\ge1,
\end{align*}
where every $P^{(0)}_j(z)$ is a polynomial of degree 
$\lfloor\frac{3j}{2}\rfloor$ and $P^{(0)}_0(z) = 1/(\sigma \sqrt{2 \pi})$.\\
The remainder term $w_n$ satisfies
\begin{align} 
    |w_n(x)| \le \frac{C}{(1+|x|)^{r+2}}.
\end{align}

