\begin{align}
    \Phi_{\mu,L,\alpha}(t,x) = \mathbb{E} \log \iint \exp\left(\sqrt{2}\sigma\cdot w^{\pi_t}(\mathbf{h})+\sigma\cdot x - \sigma\sigma^\intercal\cdot(\pi_t(1)+L(t))\right)\mathrm{d} \mu(\sigma)\mathrm{d} \mathfrak{R}(\mathbf{h})
\end{align}
where $\pi_t = L\circ \alpha^{-1}_{[t}(\cdot) - L(t)$ and $\alpha_{[t}=\alpha \mathbf{1}_{[t,T]}$. In other words, we have $\Phi_{\mu,L,\alpha}(t,x) =\mathbf{f}_\mu(\pi_t,x,-L(t))$ for every $(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^{D}$, where $\mathbf{f}_\mu$ is given as in~(equation e.f(q),<>_q= of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

