[Theorem 43 (Kernel alignment under the factorized LAN hypothesis) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Assume \cref{ass:lan}. Then
\begin{equation}
\Ker\Lambda_\ell= \Ker\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(\ell)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr).
\end{equation}
Consequently, for $h,h'\in T$,
\begin{equation}
\Lambda_\ell h=\Lambda_\ell h' \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad h-h'\in\Ker\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(\ell)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr).
\end{equation}

