[Lem 18 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] For every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$, it holds
\begin{align} 
 \sup_{r \in [0,T]} \Bigg\{ \frac{1}{n} \sum_{x} \big[  \widehat{\mathbb{L}}_{n, \lambda}^{ \gamma} H ( \tfrac{x + q_n^r }{n}  ) \big]^{2}  \Bigg\} \leq | \lambda| K_n C(\gamma,H).
\end{align}
Moreover, if $H \in C_c^{2}(\mathbb{R})$, then the role of $C(\gamma,H)$ above is fulfilled by some constant $C(H)$ satisfying \eqref{Cinvshift}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 53 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $\bfx = (X,\bbx) \in \scrc^{\alpha}([0,T],V)$ be a rough path for some index $\alpha \in (\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{2}]$. Furthermore, let $\xi \in W$ be arbitrary, and let $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T_0],W)$ be a local solution to the RDE \eqref{RDE} with $Y_0 = \xi$ for some $T_0 \in (0,T]$. Let $s,t \in [0,T_0]$ with $s \leq t$ be arbitrary, and define the interval $I := [s,t]$. Then we have
\begin{align*}
| R_{s,t}^Y | &\leq C \Big( 1 + \| Y \|_{\alpha;I} + \| X \|_{\alpha;I} \| R^{f(Y)} \|_{2 \alpha;I}
\\ &\qquad\quad + \| \bbx \|_{2\alpha;I} ( 1 + \| Y \|_{\alpha;I} ) \Big) |t-s| + C | \bbx_{s,t} |,
\end{align*}
where the constant $C > 0$ depends on $\xi$, $\alpha$, $T$, $\| f_0 \|_{\Lip}$ and $\| f \|_{C_b^{2\alpha,2}}$.

