[Lemma lem:gapEq of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] For every $\lambda>0$ and $\beta \geq 0$, there exist unique solutions $m=m(N,L,\lambda,\beta)$ and $m_{*}=m_{*}(\lambda,\beta)$ in $(0,1)$ satisfying 
(equation e91 of the paper) and (equation e127 of the paper) respectively.  Furthermore,
\begin{equation}
  0 \leq \frac{m^{2}-m_{*}^{2}}{\lambda}\lesssim   \frac{1}{m_{*}} \cdot\frac{1}{L}+|\ln m_{*}| \cdot \frac{1}{N}.     
\end{equation}

