{"artifact_digest":"sha256:10cb1e8f623faf58a81963a6156a8ad62266d3fb14ff7d9ee20801e28859e5a1","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/10/10cb1e8f623faf58a81963a6156a8ad62266d3fb14ff7d9ee20801e28859e5a1.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:f9ca3c732778046f49941f41949744b147b28618635272cd1a9b5f9d3843aa43","bundle_entry_key":"2609-02607-lemma-31-lemma4-5","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_078","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_078.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-02607-lemma-31-lemma4-5","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: According to the $w$-equation and (equation 4.15 of the paper), we have
\begin{equation}
(w(\cdot,t)-w_{\infty})_t=\Delta(w(\cdot,t)-w_{\infty})
-(w(\cdot,t)-w_{\infty})+(u(\cdot,t)-u_{\infty}).
\end{equation}
Now the variation of constants formula associated with (equation 4.20 of the paper) represents $w-w_{\infty}$ according to
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
w(\cdot,t)-w_{\infty}= e^{(\Delta-1)(t-t_0)}(w(\cdot,t_0)-w_{\infty})+\int_{t_0}^te^{(t-s)(\Delta-1)}(u(\cdot,s)-u_{\infty}).
