[Proposition prop:DmTilLForm of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] For any $m\geqslant1,$ one has
\begin{align}
D_{m}\tilde{L}= & \sum_{\sigma\in\textcolor{black}{{\cal S}_{m}}}\frac{(-1)^{e(\sigma)}}{m^{2}{m-1 \choose e(\sigma)}}\int_{\Delta_{m}}\big[e^{x_{t_{\sigma(1)}}{\rm ad}_{{\rm e}_{1}}}({\rm e}_{2}),\nonumber \\
 & \ \ \ \big[\cdots\big[e^{x_{t_{\sigma(m-1)}}{\rm ad}_{{\rm e}_{1}}}({\rm e}_{2}),e^{x_{t_{\sigma(m)}}{\rm ad}_{{\rm e}_{1}}}({\rm e}_{2})\big]\cdots\big]\big]dy_{t_{1}}\cdots dy_{t_{m}}.
\end{align}
Here we define
\[
e(\sigma)\triangleq\#\{j=1,\cdots,m-1:\sigma(j)>\sigma(j+1)\}
\]
for each permutation $\sigma\in{\cal S}_{m}.$

[Lemma lemma-k-pts-estimate-interface-discrete of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $0 < \rho \ll 1$. There exist $\delta_0 > 0$ and an absolute constant $C>0$ such that for any $0 < \delta < \delta_0$, any $(x_1,\dots,x_k) \in D_{\delta}$ and any $(r_1,\dots,r_k) \in (0,\infty)$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mu_{\delta}^{\pm}\bigg[ \bigcap_{j=1}^{k} \{ {\operatorname{dist}}(x_j, \gamma_{\delta}) \leq r_j \}\bigg] \leq C^k \prod_{j=1}^{k} \bigg(\frac{r_j}{L(x_j) \wedge d_{\delta}(x_j)}\bigg)^{\frac{5}{8}-\rho}
    \end{equation*}
    where we have set $d_{\delta}(x):= {\operatorname{dist}}(x,\partial D_{\delta})$ and $L(x_j):= \frac{1}{2} \min_{p: j \neq p} \vert x_j - x_p \vert$.

