[Proposition 50 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For all $t \in [0,T]$ with $t \leq 1$ and all $(Y,Y') \in \bbb_t$ we have
\begin{align*}
\| \Phi_t(Y,Y') \|_{X,2\alpha;[0,t]} \leq C ( 1 + |\xi| ) t^{1-2\alpha} + C ( \interleave \mathbf{X} \interleave_{\alpha;[0,t]} + t^{\alpha} ),
\end{align*}
where the constant $C > 0$ depends on $\alpha$, $\mathbf{X}$, $\| f_0 \|_{\Lip}$ and $\| f \|_{C_b^{2\alpha,2}}$.

