[Theorem thm:entropy-collapse of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] Under the two-mode approximation, as $k\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
H(k) = x_k\Bigl(1+\log\tfrac{1}{a_3}+2L_\star k\Bigr) + O\bigl(x_k^2\log(1/x_k)\bigr),
\end{equation}
and consequently
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{H}_k = x_k\Bigl(1+\tfrac{1+\log(1/a_3)}{2L_\star k}\Bigr) + O\Bigl(\tfrac{x_k^2}{k}\log\tfrac1{x_k}\Bigr),
\end{equation}
so that $\mathcal{H}_k/x_k\to1$, and
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{H}_k = G_k\,(1+O(1/k)).
\end{equation}

[Theorem mainthm of arXiv:2605.27949, 'Yaglom limits of continuous-state branching processes in Brownian random environment \than'] For any subcritical CBBRE with branching mechanism defined by (equation bm of the paper), the Yaglom limit exists and is independent of the initial value $z$. Moreover, its Laplace transform is given by {\small\begin{eqnarray}
\mathcal L(z,\lambda)=1-\left(\frac{\gamma}{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\Theta-\frac{2{\bf m}}{\sigma^2}\right)}U\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\Theta-\frac{2{\bf m}}{\sigma^2}\right),1+\frac2\beta\left(\Theta-\frac{{\bf m}}{\sigma^2}\right),\frac{\gamma\lambda^{\beta}}{2}\right)\lambda^{\Theta-\frac{2{\bf m}}{\sigma^2}},\quad \lambda, z>0,
    \end{eqnarray}}
	where $\Theta=\frac{{\bf m}}{\sigma^2}\vee(-1),$ $\gamma=\frac{4c}{\beta\sigma^2}$ and $U$ is the Kummer function defined by
\[U(a,b,r)=\frac{1}{\Gamma(a)}\int_0^\infty \mathrm{e}^{-rt}t^{a-1}(1+t)^{b-a-1}\mathrm{d} t,\qquad a>0,b\in\mathbb R,r>0.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

