[Proposition ros1 of arXiv:2607.02742, 'Gaussian fluctuations for the parabolic Anderson model with L\'evy white noise'] Let $\Phi=\{\Phi(t,x); t\in [0,T], x\in \mathbb{R}\}$ be a predictable process such that
$\Phi\in L^2(\Omega\times [0,T]\times \mathbb{R})$. If $p\geq 2$ is such that $m_p<\infty$, then
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{E}\left|\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{R}}\Phi(t,x)L(dt,dx)\right|^p \leq \mathcal{C}_p^p \bigg\{  \mathbb{E}\left(\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{R}}|\Phi(t,x)|^2 dxdt\right)^{\frac{p}{2}}
+\mathbb{E}\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{R}}|\Phi(t,x)|^p dxdt \bigg\},
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{C}_p^p=2^{p-1}B_p^p\left(m_2^{p/2}\vee m_p\right)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop partition-function-sharpness of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Let $\beta>0$, let $\mathsf{d}/2\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}$, and assume $\mu\in L^\infty\cap\mathcal{P}({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})$.  There exist constants $c,C>0$ and $N_0\ge3$, depending on $(\beta,\mu,\mathsf{d},\mathsf{s})$, such that, for every $N\ge N_0$,
\begin{align}
{\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)
\ge C^{-1}
\begin{cases}
(\log N)^c, & \mathsf{s}=\mathsf{d}/2,\\[0.3em]
\exp\left\{c(\log N)^{2-\mathsf{d}/\mathsf{s}}\right\}, & \mathsf{d}/2<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}.
\end{cases}
\end{align}
In particular, ${\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)\to+\infty$ as $N\to\infty$ throughout $\mathsf{d}/2\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}$.

