[Definition 5 (Local Lipschitz continuity) of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] A function $f : \mc{A} \subset \mc{X} \to \mathbb{R}$ is said to be locally Lipschitz if for each $x \in \mc{A}$ there exists constant $\eta > 0$ and $\sigma > 0$ such that,
    \begin{align}
      \abs{f(x) - f(\localtest)} \leq  \eta\normtwo{x-\localtest}, \:\: \text{for all}\:\:\localtest \in \ltwohsphere(x,\sigma).
    \end{align}

