[Prop 25 of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] The set $k \cdot \ordsimp{d}$ triangulates into FK-simplices as follows:
    \begin{align} 
        k \cdot \ordsimp{d} = \bigcup_{I \subseteq \indexset{d-1}} \bigcup_{\substack{\vecbf n \in \vecbf N_{d, k} [I] \\ \permelt \in \permgrp_d [I]}} (\vecbf n + \permelt \ordsimp{d})
    \end{align}
    where $\vecbf N_{d, k} [I] \subset \ZZ^d$ and $\permgrp_d [I] \subseteq \permgrp_d$ are defined as:
    \begin{align*}
        \vecbf N_{d, k} [I] =& \bigg\{(n_1, \ldots n_d) \in \ZZ^d \>\bigg|\> k-1 \ge n_1 \ge \cdots \ge n_d \ge 0 \text{, and } (i \in I \iff n_i = n_{i+1}) \bigg\} \\
        \permgrp_d [I] =& \bigg\{ \permelt \in \permgrp_d \>\bigg|\> i \in I \implies \permelt^{-1}(i) < \permelt^{-1}(i+1) \bigg\}
    \end{align*}

