[Theorem 33 (Gubinelli) of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For each controlled rough path $$(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T],L(V,W))$$ the $W$-valued rough integral \eqref{candidate} exists, and for all $s,t \in [0,T]$ we have
\begin{align}
&\bigg| \int_s^t Y_r \, d\bfx_r - Y_s X_{s,t} - Y_s' \bbx_{s,t} \bigg|
\leq C \big( \| X \|_{\alpha} \| R^Y \|_{2 \alpha} + \| \bbx \|_{2 \alpha} \| Y' \|_{\alpha} \big) |t-s|^{3 \alpha}
\end{align}
with a constant $C > 0$ depending on $\alpha$.

