[Lem L5.2 of arXiv:2609.03848, 'The mean-field limit of the Schr\"{o}dinger-Lohe model\\ and emergent dynamics'] Let $\phi_1 = \phi_1(t)$ and $\phi_2 = \phi_2(t)$ be two global solutions to (equation E-4 of the paper) corresponding to the initial data $\phi_1^0,~\phi_2^0 \in \mbox{supp}\,\rho^0$, respectively. Then, one has
\begin{equation} 
\frac{d}{dt}  \|\phi_1(t) - \phi_2(t) \|_{\mathfrak{H}} \leq  \kappa \Big(  -\frac{1}{2} +  {\mathcal D}[\rho(t)] \Big)\| \phi_1(t) - \phi_2(t) \|_{\mathfrak{H}}, \quad t > 0. 
\end{equation}

