[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2605.13512, '2605.13512'] Fix $(x,t) \in \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R}_{+}$ and suppose that the speed function $c$ satisfies Assumption \ref{assumption: growth rates}. Then we can find deterministic functions $R_L(x,t)$ and $R_U(x,t)$ so that $-\infty < R_{L} < 0  < R_{U} < +\infty$ such that, for every $r_1 \in (-\infty, R_L]$, $r_2 \in [R_U, \infty)$ and for all $n$ large enough there exists a $C=C(x,t)$ such that 
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{P} \left\{ z^{n}_{\lfloor nx \rfloor}(nt) \neq   \zeta^{n}_{x,t}(r_{1}, r_{2}) \right\} \le e^{-C(x, t) n}.
\end{equation}

