[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2605.03100, 'Berry-Esseen bounds for multivariate martingale difference sequences in the Kolmogorov dis'] \cite[Lemma 2.3]{Kojevnikov2022}
Let $\bm{X}$ denote a $d$-dimensional Gaussian random variable with mean $\bm{0}$ and variance $\bm{\Sigma}$. Then for every $s \geq 2$, there exists a constant $C_s$ depending only on $s$, such that
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\|\bm{X}\|_{\infty}^s \leq C_s \log_+^{\frac{s}{2}}d \cdot (d_{\max}(\bm{\Sigma}))^{\frac{s}{2}};
\end{align*}
furthermore, for any $\delta \in (0,1)$, 
\begin{align*}
\|\bm{X}\|_{\infty} \lesssim \sqrt{d_{\max}(\bm{\Sigma}) \log \frac{d}{\delta}}.
\end{align*}
with probability at least $1-\delta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2603.28226, '2603.28226'] Assume that $(\mathcal F_n)_{n\ge1}$ is an $\alpha$-regular atomic filtration. Let $f\in L^1(\Omega,\mathbb P)$ with $f\ge0$, and set $f_n=\mathbb E_n[f]$. Then for every $n\ge2$,
\begin{equation}

 f_n\le \alpha^{-1}f_{n-1}
 \qquad\text{a.s.}
\end{equation}

