[Lemm 20 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] Let $(\psi_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be any continuous deterministic trajectory valued in the space $\mathcal{H}^6_{\mathrm{Sym}}(\mathbb{S})$, such that $|\langle \psi_t, e_k\rangle| \leq Ck^{-6} .$ Then, the quantity
\begin{align}
\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\int_0^t \langle \psi_s,e_k\rangle\mathrm{d}\langle \mathscr{J}_s,e_k\rangle,
\end{align}
is well defined.

