body:
[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2506.20411, 'Maximal Counts in the Stopped Occupancy Problem'] Each point process $\widehat{\rm R}_{n,r}, r\in {\mathbb Z}_{>0},$ is  Poisson, with the  intensity measure
\begin{align}
{\mathbb E}[\widehat{\rm R}_{n,r}({\rm d}t)]=np_{r-1}(t){\rm d}t, ~t\geq0,
\end{align}
or, equivalently,
\begin{align}
{\mathbb E}[\widehat{\rm R}_{n,r}[t,\infty]]=n {P}_{r-1}(t), ~t\geq0.
\end{align}

