[Proposition prop:ito-sums of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $X:[0,T]\to E$ be a finite-variation pure-jump c\`adl\`ag{} path, constant between jumps, with jumps $z_a=\Delta X_{\tau_a}$ at $0<\tau_1<\cdots<\tau_n\le T$, and let $\mathrm{Sig}^I(X)$ be its forward lift
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}^I_{0,t}=\mathbf 1+\int_{(0,t]}\mathrm{Sig}^I_{0,u^-}\otimes\,\mathrm{d} X_u .
\end{equation}
Then for every word $w=(i_1,\ldots,i_k)$,
\begin{equation}
\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^I(X)_{0,T}}{w}
=\sum_{1\le a_1<\cdots<a_k\le n}z_{a_1}^{i_1}\cdots z_{a_k}^{i_k}
=\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^{\mathrm{sum}}(z)}{w},
\qquad
\mathrm{Sig}^{\mathrm{sum}}(z)=\overrightarrow{\textstyle\prod}_{a=1}^n(\mathbf 1+z_a).

\end{equation}
In particular $\mathrm{Sig}^I(X)$ is a character on the quasi-shuffle Hopf algebra.

