[Prop Prop-Half-Line-Representation of arXiv:2609.01964, 'The critical exponent for the two-dimensional semilinear wave equation with strong damping'] Let $u$ be a mild Sobolev solution on $[0,T]$ arising from compactly supported smooth initial data, where $0<T<T_{\max}$. Then, for every $0\leqslant t\leqslant T$ and $r>0$, one has
	\begin{align}
		w(t,r)\geqslant W_{\mathrm{lin}}(t,r)+\int_0^t\int_0^\infty D(t-s,r,\rho)\rho^{\frac{1-p}{2}}|w(s,\rho)|^p\,\mathrm{d}\rho\,\mathrm{d} s.
	\end{align}

