[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] For any \(n\geq 1\), under \(P(\cdot \given S_0=0)\), the vector \((S_0,S_1,\dots,S_n)\) is a centred Gaussian vector with covariances
    \begin{equation*}
        E(S_iS_j\given S_0=0) = \beta i,\quad 0\leq i \leq j \leq n.
    \end{equation*}
    Moreover, for \(n\geq 2\), under \(P(\cdot \given S_0 =0 = S_n )\), the vector \((S_0,S_1,\dots,S_n)\) is a centred Gaussian vector with covariances
    \begin{equation*}
        E(S_iS_j\given S_0 =0=S_n) = \beta \frac{i(n-j)}{n},\quad 0\leq i \leq j \leq n.
    \end{equation*}

[Proposition idrepflow of arXiv:2411.06827, 'The Exponential Lie Series and a Chen--Strichartz Formula for L{\'e}vy Processes'] The flowmap $\varphi$ has the representation
\begin{equation}
	\varphi=\mu\otimes\bar{\mu}(\mathrm{Id})=\mu\otimes\bar{\mu} \biggl(\sum_{w^0} w^0\otimes \overline w^0\biggr),
\end{equation}
where the sum is taken over all words in $({\mathbb A}^0)^\ast$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

