[Lemma lem:Jordan2_lower_tail_lower_bound of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For the Jordan-$2$ ordering $\widehat{\sigma}_2$, there exist positive constants $C$, $\delta$ such that for any $n\geq 1$, any vertex $v \in[n]$ and any $S\in[1, \delta\sqrt{v}]$ 

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}\Big(\widehat{\sigma}_2(v)\leq \frac{1}{S}v\Big) \geq  \frac{C}{S^2}.
    \end{equation}

