[Lemma eq:reweight_by_two of arXiv:2506.10765, 'A General Coupling for Ising Models and Beyond'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite  graph. Let $A\subset V$ with $|A|$ even (could be $0$). Then, $\forall \omega\in\{0,1\}^E$,
\begin{align}
2^{\abs{\omega}} (\ell^A_x \cup \mathbb{P}_p)[\omega] \propto \left(\ell^A_{\frac{2x}{1+p}} \cup \mathbb{P}_{\frac{2p}{1+ p}}\right)[\omega].
\end{align}
   In particular, with the usual $t=(t_e)_{e\in E}$ and $J=(J_e)_{e\in E}$, it holds that
\begin{align}
       2^{\abs{\omega}} (\ell^A_t \cup \mathbb{P}_{t^2})[\omega] \propto \mathbf{P}^A_{2J}.
   \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem asymptotics_f1 of arXiv:2508.04954, 'Conditional exponential directed last passage percolation under a one-point upper large de'] Let $z_c$ be a critical point of $\mathrm G(z)$. 
Then, for every $\epsilon \in (0, 1/2)$, there exists a constant $L_0>0$ such that for all $L>L_0$ and $|w|\leq L^{\epsilon/3}$, 
\begin{equation} 
    {\mathsf{f}}_{L}( z_c + w L^{-1/2}) 
    = {\mathsf{f}}_{L}( z_c) e^{\frac{1}2 \mathrm G''(z_c)  w^2 + \mathrm H'(z_c) w}
    \big(1 + O(L^{-1/2+\epsilon}) \big).

\end{equation}

