[Lemma lem:trees of arXiv:2609.02234, 'An $n(\log n)^{o(1)}$ bound for nested cycles without geometric crossings'] For every $i\in[q]$ and $\xi\in\{-,+\}$, there is a complete $b$-ary tree $T_i^\xi$ of depth $h$ rooted at $r_i^\xi$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
  \item every vertex of $T_i^\xi$ at depth $t$ lies in $W_{t+1}$, for $0\le t\le h$; and
  \item the $2q$ trees are pairwise vertex-disjoint.
\end{enumerate}
Each tree has exactly $s=b^h$ leaves, all at depth $h$.

[Theorem kappa-p of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Suppose that the hypotheses (equation VL4 of the paper)--(equation VL5' of the paper) are in force. Suppose moreover that Assumption (ass:Boltz of the paper) is satisfied with $p'\geq 4$ and that
