\begin{equation}
 \lambda_p(G)\ge
 \begin{cases}
 c_p[T_G\log(en)^{1/(p-1)}]^{-1},&1<p<2,\\
 (2T_G)^{-1},&p=2,\\
 c_pT_G^{-1},&p>2.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.30638, 'On compact steady pluriclosed soliton surfaces'] Let \((M,J)\) be a primary Hopf surface, and let \(G\) denote the identity component of its automorphism group. Then 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{rank}_c(G)=\begin{cases}
3, & \lambda=0,\\
2, & \lambda\neq0.
\end{cases}
    \end{equation}

