[Corollary eq:coexistence-ratio of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:coexistence}
Fix \(p\ge3\), \(\sigma>1\), and let \(\mu_{p,\sigma}\) be the law from
(thm:counterexample of the paper).  For every fixed \(L,\varepsilon>0\),
\(V\in\mathcal V_{2p}\), and either \(f\in\mathcal F_{2p}\) or
\(f=\ell_\eta\) for fixed \(\eta>0\),
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\mathbb E_{\mu_{p,\sigma}}\mathcal Z_{N,L}^J(V,\varepsilon,f)}
 {\mathbb E\mathcal Z_{N,L}^G(V,\varepsilon,f)}
 \longrightarrow1.
\end{equation}
The same holds for the point-incoherent functional.  Nevertheless, for
the compact interval \(B\) supplied by (thm:counterexample of the paper),
\begin{equation}
 \liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \mathbb E_{\mu_{p,\sigma}}\operatorname{Crt}_N^J(B)
 >
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log\mathbb E\operatorname{Crt}_N^G(B).
\end{equation}
Both conclusions, as well as the local-maximum and local-minimum
versions of (equation eq:coexistence-exact of the paper), remain valid for the standard
symmetric-coordinate model (equation eq:symmetric-coordinate-model of the paper).

[Lemma lem:SecondMoment of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] The second moment of $S_n(\varepsilon)$ is given by
        \begin{equation*}
            \E S_n(\varepsilon)^2 = 2^n \sum_{k=0}^n \binom{n}{k} \P{\left\lVert\ifblank{X_k}{\:\cdot\:}{X_k}\right\rVert \leq \frac{\varepsilon}{\sqrt{n}},\left\lVert\ifblank{Y_k}{\:\cdot\:}{Y_k}\right\rVert \leq \frac{\varepsilon}{\sqrt{n}}},
        \end{equation*}
        where $X_k,Y_k$ are two $m \times m$ GOE matrices having correlation $\rho_k = 1 - 2k/n$.

