[Lem 27 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 4$. There exists $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every $n\geq 1$, there exists $S\subset \Lambda_n$ containing $0$ which satisfies the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}
	\item[$(i)$] $\varphi_{\beta_c}(S)\leq C(\log n)^{\mathds{1}_{d=4}}$;
	\item[$(ii)$] one has
	\begin{equation}
		\beta_c \sum_{\substack{x\in S\cap \Lambda_{n/2}\\y\notin S\\x\sim y}}\langle \sigma_0\sigma_x\rangle_{S,\beta_c}\langle\sigma_0\sigma_y\rangle_{\beta_c}\leq C\frac{(\log n)^{\mathds{1}_{d=4}}}{n^{d-2}}.
	\end{equation} 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:RFGbound of arXiv:2604.28068, 'Mean-square Stability and Bifurcations for Dissipative SDEs'] Suppose Assumptions~(assum:FG_bounds of the paper) and (ass:dissipative of the paper) hold and let $Y$ be the solution of (equation eq:main_YSDE of the paper).
Then there exists a positive constant $K_{x^\ast}>0$, which depends on $x^\ast$, such that 
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|R_F(Y(t),x^\ast)\right\|^2\right]\leq K_{x^\ast} \left(1+R_{q_1+2}+\|X_0\|^{2(q_1+2)}\right),
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
\expect{\left\|\mathrm{R_G}(Y(t),x^\ast)\right\|_{\mathbf F}^2} \leq K_{x^\ast} \left(1+R_{q_2+2}+\|X_0\|^{2(q_2+2)}\right), 
\end{equation*}
where $q_1$ and $q_2$ are the exponents in Assumption~(assum:FG_bounds of the paper) and $R_q$ is defined in Lemma (lem:dissipativemomentbound of the paper).

