[Lemma lem:BoundedDrift of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Suppose that $\alpha \ll (rm)^{-1/2}$. Then for $t \in \mathbb{N}$,
        \begin{equation*}
            \E[t]{\Phi_t - \Phi_{t-1} \mid \Phi_{t-1} = x} \leq
            \begin{cases}
                O(m^{-1}) & \text{if}~x \leq 2m, \\
                -\Omega(m^{-2})x & \text{if}~x \geq 2m,
            \end{cases}
        \end{equation*}
        where the implicit constants depend only on the parameters $\eta$ and $\theta$.

