[Proposition prop:CTL for W of arXiv:2606.28031, 'Insurance risk models in a heterogeneous time-dependent population: scaling limits and rui'] Under Assumptions~(A:hyp LLN for W of the paper) and~(A:hyp TCL for W of the paper), if  $X(1)$ and $Y(1)$ have finite second moments, then
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{\sqrt{t}}\PAR{W(t)-\mathbb{E}[W(t)]}\overset{\rm d}{\underset{t\to \infty}{\longrightarrow}}\mathscr{Z}^{\rm i}.
\end{equation}

