    \widetilde{\otimes}_{\pi}^{\,N}
 X_i$ contains a non-elementary exposed point. 

    \item[(b)] There exists a real Banach space $F_N$ such that $B_{
    \widetilde{\otimes}_{\pi_s}^{N, \,s}
{F_N}}$ contains an exposed point which is not of the form $\pm z^{\otimes N}$.
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Lemma convergence of tilde mu n t of arXiv:2411.09260, 'The Hydrodynamic Limit of Hawkes Processes on Adaptive Stochastic Networks'] For any $\epsilon > 0$, define the event
 \begin{align}
\mathcal{U}^n_{\epsilon} = \bigg\lbrace  d_W\big( \tilde{\mu}^n_{T} , \mu_T \big) \leq \epsilon \bigg\rbrace  .
 \end{align}
 Then for any $\epsilon > 0$,
 \begin{align}
 \underset{n\to\infty}{\overline{\lim}} n^{-1}\log \mathbb{P}\big(  (\mathcal{U}^n_{\epsilon})^c \big) < 0. 
 \end{align}
Furthermore, for any $\epsilon > 0$, 
 \begin{align}
 \underset{n\to\infty}{\overline{\lim}} n^{-1} \log \mathbb{P}\bigg(  \sup_{j\in I_n} \sup_{t\leq T} \sup_{a\in \Gamma_E , \alpha\in\Gamma} \big| \tilde{G}^{j}_{t}(\alpha,a)- \hat{G}^j_{t}(\alpha,a) \big| > \epsilon \bigg) < 0. 
 \end{align}

[Proposition 4 (Kallianpur-Striebel formula) of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] If a random variable $U$ is independent of $W$ under $P$ and \( E[|U|] < \infty \), then it holds that
\begin{align}

  E[U|\mathcal{Y}_t^\epsilon] =
  \frac{\displaystyle E_{Q^\epsilon}\left[ U Z_t^\epsilon \middle| \mathcal{Y}_t^\epsilon \right]}
       {\displaystyle E_{Q^\epsilon}\left[ Z_t^\epsilon \middle| \mathcal{Y}_t^\epsilon \right]}
  \quad (0 \leq t \leq T).
\end{align}

