[Lem lem 4.10 of arXiv:2411.01847, 'Well-Posedness of Stochastic Chemotaxis System'] Suppose $g$ satisfies condition ((g of the paper)) with $\mu>\frac{\chi}{2}$. Then, there exists a constant $C_{\|u_0\|_\infty}>0$ such that for all $T>0$, we have
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb{E}\sup_{t\in  [0,T\wedge\tau]}\|u(t)\|_\infty \leq C_{\|u_0\|_\infty}.
\end{align*}

