[Prop 22 of arXiv:2608.26642, '2608.26642'] For $y\in \R$, we have
\begin{align}
\mathscr{L} h(\cdot-y)=\delta_y,
\end{align}
that is, for $f\in C_c^\infty(\R)$, we have
\begin{align}
\int_\R h(x-y)\widehat{\mathscr{L}}f(x)\,dx=f(y).
\end{align}

