body:
[Lemma lmm:complementary scaling of arXiv:2411.10311, 'Planar Novikov-Shubin invariant for adjacency matrices of structured directed dense random'] There is a constant $C>0$, such that uniformly for all $\tau \le \rho(S)/2$ the polynomial bounds 
\bels{power law bound}{
\tau^C \lesssim v \lesssim \tau^{-C}\,,\qquad  \tau^C \lesssim w \lesssim \tau^{-C},
}
are satisfied. Furthermore,  
\bels{v average scaling}{
\widetilde{v}_k\sim \avg{\widetilde{v}_k} \sim \frac{1}{\widetilde{w}_k} \sim \frac{1}{\avg{\widetilde{w}_k}} \,, 
}
hold true for all $k \in \llbracket L \rrbracket$  and 
\bels{monotonicity for v}{
\avg{\widetilde{v}_k} \lesssim \avg{\widetilde{v}_l}\,, \qquad \avg{\widetilde{w}_l} \lesssim \avg{\widetilde{w}_k}\qquad \text{ for all }\; k \LHD l\,.
} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

