[Definition 187 (The $\nullhyparg{u}$-tangent elliptic-hyperbolic characteristic current) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\SigmatTan$ be a $\Sigma_t$-tangent vectorfield.
	We define the characteristic current
	to be the vectorfield $\ehcurrent = \ehcurrent[\SigmatTan,\pmb{\partial} \SigmatTan]$
	with the following components, $(\alpha = 0,1,2,3)$:
	\begin{align} 
		\ehcurrent^{\alpha}[\SigmatTan,\pmb{\partial} \SigmatTan]
		& \eqdef 
		\SigmatTan^{\gamma} 
		\Nullhypersurfaceproject_{\gamma}^{\ \beta} 
		\Nullhypersurfaceproject_{\kappa}^{\ \alpha} \partial_{\beta} \SigmatTan^{\kappa}
		-
		\SigmatTan^{\gamma} \Nullhypersurfaceproject_{\gamma}^{\ \alpha} 
		\Nullhypersurfaceproject_{\beta}^{\ \kappa}
		\partial_{\kappa} \SigmatTan^{\beta}.
	\end{align}

[Theorem theorem 1.1 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{3}$ be a smoothly bounded domain and $\ell\geq0$. Then there exists  $C(K)>0$ with the property that whenever $u_0, v_0$ and $w_0$ fulfill (equation 1.2 of the paper) and (equation 1.6 of the paper), the problem (equation 1.1 of the paper) admits a
 continuous global weak  solution $(u,v,w)$  in the sense of Definition (Definition 2.1 of the paper) below, which is such that
    \begin{equation}
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
&u\in C^{0}_{loc}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))\cap L^{\infty}_{loc}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))\\
&v\in C^{0}_{loc}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))\cap C^{2,1}_{loc}(\overline{\Omega}\times (0,\infty))\cap L^{\infty}_{loc}([0,\infty);W^{1,\infty}(\Omega))\\
&w\in C^{0}_{loc}(\overline{\Omega}\times [0,\infty))\cap C^{2,1}_{loc}(\overline{\Omega}\times (0,\infty))\\
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{equation}
and that  $u\geq0, v>0$ and $w>0$ on $\overline{\Omega}\times(0,\infty)$, and that
\begin{equation}
    \|u(\cdot,t)\|_{L^\infty(\Omega)}+\|v(\cdot,t)\|_{W^{1,\infty}(\Omega)}+\|w(\cdot,t)\|_{W^{1,\infty}(\Omega)}\leq C(K)~~\mbox{for all}~~t>0.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

