body:
[Corollary 22 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Assume \eqref{H1} and \eqref{eq:3rd}. For any $\delta>0$ and $m\ge 1$, uniformly for $\delta n \le s \le h(q_n)-\delta n$, we have:
        \begin{gather}
            \p_n\Big(\mathfrak{p}(u_{1}^{s+1}),\ldots, \mathfrak{p}(u_{m}^{s+1})~\text{are  distinct}\Big)=1-\dfrac{\binom{m}{2}\sigma_n(s)^2}{q_n(s)}\big(1+o_n(1)\big);      \\
            \p_n\Big(\{\mathfrak{p}(u_{1}^{s+1})=\mathfrak{p}(u_{2}^{s+1})\}\cap\{ \mathfrak{p}(u_{2}^{s+1}),\ldots, \mathfrak{p}(u_{m}^{s+1})~\text{are  distinct}\}\Big)
            =\,\frac{1}{q_n(s)} \big(\sigma_n(s)^2 + o_n(1)\big).       
        \end{gather}

