body:
[Theorem 30 (Coordinate criterion for strict coarse-depth loss) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Fix $m<r$ and assume exact depth $r$ at $\theta_0$ together with \cref{ass:regularity}. Let $T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$ be a tangent block and let $T_0\subset T$ be a linear subspace of dimension $p\ge1$. Assume
\begin{equation}
\rank\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(r)}(\theta_0)|_{T_0}\bigr)=p.
\end{equation}
Let $I$ be a finite family of visible state / appended-edge pairs as above, and let $M_I:=D\Phi_I^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_{T_0}$.
If
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\alph*)}]
\item \begin{equation*}
\Ker(M_I)\subset\Ker\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_{T_0}\bigr),
\end{equation*}
\item \begin{equation*}
\rank(M_I)<p,
\end{equation*}
\end{enumerate}
then the depth-$m$ window is not first-order locally sufficient relative to depth $r$ on $T_0$.

