[Corollary cor-detprocessexplicit of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Let $L=(L_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a Lévy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) and let $D=(D_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the determinant process of its stochastic exponential defined in (equation eq-detprocess of the paper). Then 
	\begin{align*}
		D_t&= \exp\Bigg(\operatorname{tr}(L_t) -  \frac12 \sum_{m,n=1}^d \sigma_{(m,n),(n,m)} \cdot t  \Bigg) \prod_{0<s\leq t} \det\big((\Id+\Delta L_s) e^{-\Delta L_s}\big), \quad t\geq 0.
	\end{align*}

