[Definition 2 (Regular Lagrangian flow) of arXiv:2607.25685, 'Mimicking diffusion processes with differential equations'] $Z:[0,T]\times\R^d\to\R^d$ is a \emph{regular Lagrangian flow} (RLF) for a velocity field $v$ if
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] for $\Leb$-a.e.\ $x$, $t\mapsto Z(t,x)$ is absolutely continuous with
$Z(t,x)=x+\int_0^tv(Z(s,x),s)\dd s$;
\item[(ii)] $Z(t,\cdot)_\#\Leb\le L\,\Leb$ for some $L\ge1$.
\end{enumerate}

