[Theorem of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] We assume that there exists $\beta_c \in \mathbb R_+^*$ such that $ \theta(\beta) = 0$ for all $\beta \in ]0, \beta_c[$ and $ \theta(\beta) > 0$ for all $\beta \in ]\beta_c, +\infty[$. Then,
  \begin{itemize}
    \item for all $\beta \in ]0, \beta_c[$ there exists $c_\beta > 0$ such that for any $n$ large enough, $\theta_n(\beta) \leqslant \exp(- c_\beta n)$;
    \item there exists $c, \delta > 0$ such that $ \theta(\beta) \geqslant c (\beta - \beta_c)$ for all $\beta \in [\beta_c, \beta_c + \delta[$.
  \end{itemize}

