[Theorem 2DHD-lemma6.13 of arXiv:2604.21591, '\bf Long-time dynamics of stochastic 2D hydrodynamic-type evolution equations driven by mu'] Under the hypotheses of Lemma (2DHD-lemma6.11 of the paper). For the $\mathscr{D}$-pullback measure attractor $\mathscr{A}=\{\mathscr{A}(\tau):\tau\in \mathbb{R}\}$ of 
	system (equation 2DHD-1.1 of the paper) and the measure attractor $\mathscr{A}_{\infty}$ of system (equation 2DHD-asy1.1 of the paper), it holds
\begin{align*}
	\lim\limits_{\tau\rightarrow -\infty}d_{\mathcal{P}_4(H)}(\mathscr{A}(\tau),\mathscr{A}_{\infty})=0.
\end{align*}

[Lemma hnlb of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:geq1 of the paper) is satisfied and integers $1\leq a<b<\infty$. Then, 
\begin{equation} 
h_b^+(\mathbf x)-h^+_{a-1}(\mathbf x)=\sum_{i=a}^b \mathbbm{1}_{\{x_i=1\}}\frac{1}{A_i(\mathbf x)} \geq \log\Big(\frac{b}{2a}\Big). 
\end{equation} 
In particular, with $a=1$ and $b=n$ we obtain~(equation eq:hn+lb of the paper).

