[Definition Height function associated with a couple of arXiv:2412.04032, 'Cutoff for the mixing time of the Facilitated Exclusion Process'] Let $(Y, \sigma) \in \mathbb{Z} \times \Gamma_{K,P}$. The map to a height function is defined as
\begin{equation}
 	\Psi:
    \begin{cases}
        \mathbb{Z} \times \Gamma_{K,P} \to \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{T}_K}\\
        (Y,\sigma) \mapsto  \zeta,
    \end{cases}       
    \end{equation}
where
 \begin{equation}
    \begin{cases}
        \zeta_0 =\zeta_K = - Y\\
        \zeta_k = \zeta_{k-1} +  \sigma_k-\frac{P}{K} \quad \forall \, 1\le k<K.
    \end{cases}       
