[Lem lm1 of arXiv:2411.01849, 'A tamed-adaptive Milstein scheme for stochastic differential equations with low regularity'] For any $p \in [2, p_0]$, there exists a positive constant $C= C(p, \gamma, \eta)$ such that for any $t \geq 0,$
\begin{align*} 
\mathbb{E}[\vert X_t\vert ^p| \mathcal{F}_{\underline{t}}] \leq |X_{\underline{t}}|^p+ C(t- \underline{t})\left(1+|X_{\underline{t}}|^p\right).
\end{align*}

