[Definition def:generalversionXY of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given an integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, a collection of non-negative conductances $\left( J_{xy,k} \right)_{\{ x, y\} \in E(\Lambda_L), 1 \leq k \leq n}$, and a parameter $\lambda > 0$, we define the generalised XY model to be the probability distribution on the set $\Omega_{\Lambda_L}^{\mathrm{div-}\mathbb{S}^1}$ given by the identity
    \begin{equation} 
        \mu_{\Lambda_L , J, \lambda}^{\mathrm{XY}} (d \theta) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda_L, J, \lambda}^{\mathrm{XY}}} \exp \left( \lambda \cos(\theta_{0g}) \right) \exp \left( \sum_{x \sim y} \sum_{1 \leq k \leq n} J_{xy,k} \cos(\theta_{xy, k}) \right) d \theta.
    \end{equation}
    We denote by $\left\langle \cdot \right\rangle_{L , J, \lambda}^{\mathrm{XY}}$ the expectation with respect to this measure.

[Definition 10 of arXiv:2606.31455, 'Discrete time-multidimensional renewal theory and applications'] Let $f:\mathbb{N}^d\to[0,1]$ be a pmf and let $b:\mathbb{N}^d\to\mathbb{R}$ be given.
A (discrete) multi-time renewal equation is of the form

\begin{equation}
g=b+f*g,
\end{equation}

where $g:\mathbb{N}^d\to\mathbb{R}$ is the unknown.

