[Proposition prop_tight of arXiv:2412.07258, 'Permuton limit of a generalization of the Mallows and $k$-card-minimum models'] For any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$ and $K \in \mathbb{R}_+$ we have
\begin{equation}
  \max_{1 \leqslant i \leqslant \lfloor (1-\varepsilon)n \rfloor} \; \max_{j \in [n]} \; \mathbb{P}\left( |Z_{i,j}^n| \geqslant (K+1)\cdot L(\varepsilon) \cdot e^{L(\varepsilon)}+K \right) \leqslant \frac{1}{K^2},
\end{equation}

