body:
[Lem local-drop-comparison of arXiv:2609.03856, 'Consensus time for asynchronous $\ell^p$ relaxation: graph dependence'] Let $q=p/(p-1)$.  There is $c_p>0$ such that, for every profile $f$ and
vertex $u$ of degree $d$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal{D}_p(f,u)\ge c_p
 \begin{cases}
 \displaystyle\max\left\{
  \frac{B_f(u)^2}{A_f(u)},
  \frac{|B_f(u)|^q}{d^{1/(p-1)}}\right\},&1<p<2,\\[3mm]
 \displaystyle\min\left\{
  \frac{B_f(u)^2}{A_f(u)},
  \frac{|B_f(u)|^q}{d^{1/(p-1)}}\right\},&p\ge2.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}
All expressions are understood by the conventions above.  In particular,
the estimate remains valid when some incident edge differences vanish.

