[Corollary coro_1 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $A$ be a symmetric matrix. For every $\epsilon>0$ and integer $m\geq2$, 
\begin{eqnarray}

\Pr(\boldsymbol{\Delta}>t)\leq \inf_{0<b<1}e^{\Lambda_m(t,b)}\leq (1+\epsilon)\exp\bigg(-\tilde{\kappa}_{m}\min\bigg\{\frac{t^{1+\frac{1}{m}}}{\|A\|_{m+1}^{1+\frac{1}{m}}}, \frac{t}{\|A\|}\bigg\}\bigg),
\end{eqnarray} 
where $\tilde{\kappa}_{m}>0$ is a constant that depends only on $m, n$ and $\epsilon$.

