[Proposition Propositio:Stabilitytrace of arXiv:2609.00324, 'Quantitative Stability for Fractional Yamabe minimizers'] Let $\gamma \in (0,1)$ and $a= 1-2\gamma$. Then, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $U\in \dot{W}^{1,2}(\mathbb{R}_{+}^{n+1}, y^a )$ with trace $TU =w$
\begin{align*}
    \int_{\mathbb{R}_{+}^{n+1}} y^a |\nabla U|^2 dxdy - \frac{1}{\bar{S}(n,\gamma)} \|w \|_{L^{2^{*}}(\mathbb{R}^n )}^2  \geq C \text{dist} (U,\mathcal{M}_{\mathbb{R}_+^{n+1}})^2 \, ,
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align*}
    \text{dist} (U,\mathcal{M}_{\mathbb{R}_+^{n+1}}) = \inf \{\|U - V\|_{\dot{W}^{1,2}(\mathbb{R}^{n+1}_+,y^a)} : V \in \mathcal{M}_{\mathbb{R}^{n+1}_+ } \} .
\end{align*}

