[Proposition 47 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:basic}, for all sufficiently large $N$, if $z,\zeta\in\C^+$ satisfy
        \begin{align}
                z=\Phi_t(\zeta), 
        \end{align}
        then
        \begin{align}
                \Pi(z)= \begin{pmatrix}a_t(\zeta)I_M & 0   \\
               0             & I_N\end{pmatrix} \Pi_0(\zeta) \begin{pmatrix}I_M & 0                  \\
               0   & a_t(\zeta)^{-1}I_N\end{pmatrix}. 
        \end{align}
        In particular,
        \begin{align}
                m(z)=a_t(\zeta)^{-1}m_0(\zeta), \qquad g(z)=a_t(\zeta)(g_0(\zeta)+th_0(\zeta)). 
        \end{align}
        Hence $m_{\rm fc}=m$, and the rectangular free convolution of $\bnu_0$ with the Mar\v{c}enko--Pastur law at time $t$ and aspect ratio $c_N$ coincides with $\bnu$.

