[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2609.03954, 'Galois representations ramified at one prime via relative deformation theory'] Put
\begin{equation}
        q=A+s+C.
\end{equation}
For every $\alpha\in\mathcal B$, the image of $\rho_{2A}^*$ contains
an element lying in the $q$-th congruence subgroup whose leading term
at level $q$ is $X_\alpha$.  Moreover
\begin{equation}
        q+1\le2A-R.
