[Lemma 6 (Exponential Young convolution) of arXiv:2608.08177, 'Uniform-in-Time Smoluchowski--Kramers Approximation\\ in Total Variation for Fractional SD'] Let $w\in C^\gamma([0,\infty))$, $\gamma\in(0,1)$, and
\[
  R_t^\mu(w)=\int_0^t e^{-(t-s)/\mu}\,dw_s.
\]
For every $t\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 |R_t^\mu(w)|
 \le C_\gamma\mu^\gamma
 \sum_{j=0}^{\lfloor t\rfloor}
 e^{-j/(2\mu)}
 [w]_{\gamma;I_{t,j}},
\end{equation}
where
$I_{t,j}=[(t-j-1)\vee0,(t-j)\vee0]$ and empty intervals are omitted.
Consequently, if $w=B^H$ and $p\ge1$, then
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\ge0}\norm{R_t^\mu(B^H)}_{L^p(\Omega)}
  \le C_{p,\gamma,H}\mu^\gamma.
\end{equation}

