\begin{align*}
 \{r-i\}\{r+n+i\}
 &=(q^{r-i}-q^{-r+i})(q^{r+n+i}-q^{-r-n-i})\\
 &=q^{2r+n}+q^{-2r-n}-q^{2i+n}-q^{-2i-n},
\end{align*}
which is \eqref{eq:node-factorization}.  If $r,i\ge0$ and the
right-hand side vanishes in $\Bbbk$, then one quantum integer is zero.
