[Lemma lem:size_cluster_origin_complment_infinitecomponent of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Let $p>p'$ for some $p'$ close enough to 1. There exists a dimension-dependent constant~$a>0$ such that,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{P}_p (|\mathcal{V}_0|\ge M) \le \exp(- a \cdot M^{(d-1)/d} ) \quad \text{for } M \text{ large enough.} 
    \end{equation}

[Lemma lem:layering of arXiv:2609.02234, 'An $n(\log n)^{o(1)}$ bound for nested cycles without geometric crossings'] Let $G$ be a graph, let $r\ge2$ be an integer, and let $\beta_r=1+(r-1)^{-1}\sum_{j=1}^{r-2}(8r)^j$. If
\begin{equation}
\delta(G)\ge16r\log(8\beta_r),
\end{equation}
then $G$ contains pairwise disjoint sets $W_0,W_1,\ldots,W_{r-1}$ such that $e(G[W_0])\ge e(G)/8$ and
\[
  d_G(v,W_{j+1})\ge\frac{d_G(v)}{8r}\qquad\text{for all $0\le j\le r-2$ and all $v\in W_j$.}
\]
Moreover, for every $r\ge8$ the condition $\delta(G)\ge32r^2\log r$ implies (equation eq:layer-threshold of the paper).

