[Lemma of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] An $X\in{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-lvl}$ is $S$-local precisely if it is a $G$-global $\Omega$-spectrum.
    \begin{proof}
        By adjunction, $X$ is $S$-local if and only if $\varphi^*X$ is local with respect to the maps $\smash{\textup{const}\,\kappa_{V,W}^{H,H}}$ for all $\varphi\colon H\to G$ and all representations $V,W$. If we fix a faithful $H$-representation $U$, then the collapse map $\textbf{\textup{L}}(U,-)_+\smashp\textbf{\textup{O}}(V,-)\to\textbf{\textup{O}}(V,-)$ is $G$-global level weak equivalence by Proposition~(prop:smash-well-based of the paper) applied levelwise, and likewise for $\textbf{\textup{L}}(U,-)_+\smashp\textbf{\textup{O}}(V\oplus W,-)\smashp S^W\to\textbf{\textup{O}}(V\oplus W,-)\smashp S^W$; thus, being local with respect to the map $\kappa_{V,W}^{H,H}$ is equivalent to being local with respect to $\textbf{\textup{L}}(U,-)_+\smashp\kappa_{V,W}^{H,H}$ (in the $\infty$-categorical sense). We now observe that $\textbf{\textup{L}}(U,-)_+\smashp\textbf{\textup{O}}(V,-)$ is cofibrant in $\cat{$\bm H$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Sp}$ by the explicit description of the generating cofibrations, as is $\textbf{\textup{L}}(U,-)_+\smashp\textbf{\textup{O}}(V\oplus W,-)$. Since $S^W$ is an $H$-CW-complex, the endofunctor $\Omega^W$ of $\cat{$\bm H$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Sp}$ is right Quillen by Lemma~(lemma:G-Top*-tensored of the paper) applied levelwise, so that ${-}\smashp S^W$ is left Quillen; we conclude that ${\textbf{\textup{L}}(U,-)_+\smashp\kappa_{V,W}^{H,H}}$ is a map of cofibrant objects. Lemma~(lemma:localization-on-homs of the paper) then shows that a fibrant object of $\cat{$\bm H$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Sp}$ is local in the topologically enriched sense with respect to $\smash{\textbf{\textup{L}}(U,-)_+\smashp\kappa_{V,W}^{H,H}}$ if and only if its image in ${\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\text{$H$-gl}$ is local in the $\infty$-categorical sense with respect to $\smash{\kappa_{V,W}^{H,H}}$. 

        Fixing $V$ and $W$, but letting $U$ vary and passing to colimits, we see that an object of ${\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\text{$H$-lvl}$ represented by a fibrant and levelwise closed $H$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-spectrum $Y$ is local with respect to $\textup{const}\,\kappa_{V,W}^{H,H}$ if and only if $Y(V)({\mathcal{U}}_H)^H\to \Omega^WY(V\oplus W)({\mathcal{U}}_H)^H$ is a weak homotopy equivalence for our favourite complete $H$-universe ${\mathcal{U}}_H$. As the latter condition is invariant under $H$-global level weak equivalences of levelwise closed $H$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-spectra, we conclude that this more generally holds without the fibrancy assumption. Varying $\varphi\colon H\to G$ and the $H$-representations $V$ and $W$, Lemma~(lemma:omega-fewer-quantifiers of the paper) then shows that a levelwise closed $X\in\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Sp}$ defines an $S$-local object of ${\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\text{$G$-gl}$ if and only if it is a $G$-global $\Omega$-spectrum. As any $X\in\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Sp}$ is weakly equivalent to a levelwise closed $G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-spectrum (Corollary~(cor:cofibrant-LSp-closed of the paper)), this completes the proof. 
    \end{proof}

[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.13358, 'Extreme points of sets of probability measures and $\phi$-divergences'] For $p\in \cM$, the following statements are equivalent.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $p$ is $\ll$-minimal in $\cM$.
        \item For every $p'\in\cM\setminus\{p\}$, every $q\in\cM$ with $p\ll q$, $p'\ll q$, and every convex function $\varphi\colon[0,\infty)\to\R$ satisfying 
        \begin{equation}
        \varphi(1)=0,\quad \varphi'_+(0)=-\infty,\quad \Div{\varphi}{p}{q}<\infty,\quad \Div{\varphi}{p'}{q}<\infty,
    \end{equation}
    one has
    \begin{equation}
    \lim_{\lambda\uparrow 1}\frac{\Div{\varphi}{\lambda p+(1-\lambda)p'}{q}-\Div{\varphi}{p}{q}}{1-\lambda}=-\infty.
    \end{equation}
    In particular, $\lambda=1$ is a strict local maximizer of the map
    \begin{equation*}
        [0,1]\to[0,\infty),\quad \lambda\mapsto\Div{\varphi}{\lambda p+(1-\lambda)p'}{q}.
    \end{equation*}
    \end{enumerate}

