body:
[Lem ll1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Given $x \in \mathbb{Z}^2$ and $0 < r < R$, the simple symmetric random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^2$ satisfies the following estimates:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item [a)] For any $y \in {\rm B}(x;R)\setminus {\rm B}(x;r)$, 
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{P}_y( \tau_{{\rm B}(x;r)} < \tau_{\partial {\rm B}(x;R)})  = \frac{R- \log \|x-y\| +O({\rm e}^{-r})}{R-r}.  
		\end{equation}
		\item [b)] For any $y \in {\rm B}(x;R) \setminus \{x\}$, 
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{P}_y( \tau_x < \tau_{\partial {\rm B}(x;R)}) = \left(\frac{R-\log\|x-y\|+O(\|x-y\|^{-1})}{R}\right)(1+O(R^{-1})).  
		\end{equation} 
	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

