[Lemma 5 (Lemma 3.4 in \cite{gotze2021concentration}) of arXiv:2606.24090, 'Sparsity-adaptive concentration inequalities for random polynomials'] Let $A=(a_\mathbf{i})_{\mathbf{i}\in[n]^d}$ be a $d$-tensor, $I\subseteq [d]$ and $\mathbf{i}_I\in [n]^{|I|}$ fixed. Then for any $\mathcal{K}\in \Pi_d$ and $\mathcal{J}\in \Pi(I^c)$,
    \begin{align}
        \Vert (A\circ \mathbf{1}_{L(\mathcal{K})})_{\mathbf{i}_{I^c}}\Vert_{\mathcal{J}}\le 2^{|\mathcal{K}|(|\mathcal{K}|-1)/2}\Vert A_{\mathbf{i}_{I^c}}\Vert_{\mathcal{J}}.
    \end{align}

