body:
[Lemma concavity-left of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] For $0\leq s\leq x$ we have 
\begin{equation}
p_{n}(s)\geq \frac{s}{x}\,p.  
\end{equation}
Consequently, 
\begin{equation}
\int_{0}^{x}p_{n}(s)\,ds\geq \frac{xp}{2}.  
\end{equation}

