[Proposition prop:heat_asymp of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] For $0<\alpha<2$, there exists a constant $c>0$ such that for all $x\in \mathbb G$ and $t>0$,
\begin{align}
     p^{(\alpha)}(t,x)\leqslant  \frac{ct}{\|x\|^{Q+\alpha}_\alpha}.
\end{align}
Moreover, for all $x\in\mathbb{G}$,
\begin{align}
    \lim_{t\to 0} \frac{p^{(\alpha)}(t,x)}{t}=\frac{1}{\|x\|^{Q+\alpha}_\alpha}.
\end{align}

