[Theorem k1k2Ithm of arXiv:2608.04730, 'A new look at some aspects of one-dimensional random sequential adsorption and its continu'] Let $M^{(n)}_{k_1,k_2;I}$ denote the expected number of bonded molecules under Model I in (equation models of the paper).
Then
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&m_{k_1,k_2;I}:=\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{M^{(n)}_{k_1,k_2;I}}n=m_{k_2}+\sum_{l=k_1}^{k_2-1}g_{k_2;l}M_{k_1}^{(l)},
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $m_{k_2}$ is as in Theorem (mkthm of the paper),  $g_{k;m}$ is as in Theorem (gapsthm of the paper) and $M_{k_1}^{(l)}$ is the expected number of bonded molecules under $k_1$-bonding on a row of $l$ molecules.

