{"artifact_digest":"sha256:ccbb5828480d793f1cf7b72152827f8a4bf2aaaee51c362730804ed44323003d","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/cc/ccbb5828480d793f1cf7b72152827f8a4bf2aaaee51c362730804ed44323003d.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:923847a4bdd09ce28c5f05d7a43a8b80028eb0706ca64b936e6d464e31a86004","bundle_entry_key":"2608-30382-lemma-8-inverse-moment-estimates","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_068","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_068.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-30382-lemma-8-inverse-moment-estimates","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We can assume without loss of generality that $ c = 1 $.
Note that for every $x\ge0$
\bas{
x^{-p}=\frac 1{\Gamma(p)}\int_0^\infty e^{-x\lambda } \lambda^{p-1}\,\mathrm{d} \lambda
}
so that by Fubini's theorem
\bas{
{\mathbb E}[(V_n^*)^{-p}]&=\frac 1{\Gamma(p)}  {\mathbb E}\Bigl[ \int_0^\infty e^{-V_n^* \lambda} \lambda^{p-1}\,\mathrm{d} \lambda\Bigr] =\frac 1{\Gamma(p)}  \int_0^\infty   {\mathbb E}\bigl[e^{-\lambda V_n^*}\bigr]\, \lambda^{p-1}\,\mathrm{d} \lambda.
}
