[Theorem thm:dissipation_of_E of arXiv:2602.00988, 'Wealth exchange under ceiling and flooring constraints: a modified Bennati–Dragulescu–Yako'] Let ${\bf p}(t) = \{p_n(t)\}_{n\geq 0}$ be a classical solution to the system of nonlinear ODEs (equation eq:law_limit of the paper)-(equation eq:two-classes of the paper) with ${\bf p}(0) \in \mathcal{A}$. There exist fixed $k_1>0$ and $k_2>0$ such that for all $t \geq 0$ we have
\begin{equation}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} t} \widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{ab}[{\bf p}] \leq 0.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} t} \widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{ab}[{\bf p}] = 0$ if and only if ${\bf p}$ coincides with ${\bf p}^*$ (equation eq:equi of the paper). Consequently, ${\bf p}(t) \xrightarrow{t\to \infty} {\bf p}^*$ strongly in $\ell^p$ for each $1 < p < \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

