[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2603.28170, 'Stabilization time of finite configurations with a second class particle in discrete TASEP'] For any string $\omega$ with a single $1$ in it, we have the equality of events
\begin{equation}
\{U(\omega)<K(\omega)\}=\{E_n(\omega)=0\}.
\end{equation}
Furthermore,
\begin{equation}
\{E_n(\omega)>1\}\subseteq\{U(\omega)>n-R(\omega)\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition of arXiv:2607.14792, 'On the degree distribution of large tentacular Bienaymé--Galton--Watson trees'] A rooted planar tree $\tau$ is a subset of $\mathcal{U}$ such that 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\varnothing \in \tau$,
        \item if $u = vu' \in \tau$ then $v \in \tau$,
        \item for all $u \in \tau$, there exists $c_u(\tau) \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$ such that $uj \in \tau$ if and only if $j \leq c_u(\tau)$; $c_u(\tau)$ is called the number of children of $u$ in $\tau$.
    \end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:upperbound of arXiv:2512.17808, 'Zeros of polynomial powers under the heat flow'] For any $r,t>0$, there is a constant $c>0$ such that
\begin{align*}
U_{n,t}(z)=\frac {1}  {\alpha n} \log \left\lvert {\rm e}^{-\frac{t}{2\alpha n}\partial_z^2}P^n(z)\right\rvert <c
\end{align*}
uniformly in $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and $|z|\le r\sqrt t$. The bound $c$ depends on $t$ as $c=\frac {1} {2} \max(0,\log t)+ \tilde c$ for some $\tilde c>0$, which is independent of $t$ and only depends on the data $(\lambda_j)_j, (\alpha_j)_j$ of the polynomial $P$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

