[Lemma lem.I_by_It of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For every ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m \in \mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{k}$ with $0 \leqslant h \leqslant k-2$, the following estimate holds
		\begin{equation}
			I^{\,(N,k)}_{m,\alpha, h}( i,j)  \leqslant (j+1)\sum_{\ell=0}^j \widetilde{I}^{\, (N,k)}_{m, \alpha+\ell+1, h+1}(i+\ell,j-\ell).
		\end{equation}

[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Let
        \begin{equation}
            \bar u_1(t, x) = U_*\left(x-2t + \frac{3}{2} \log t\right) + \frac{\gamma}{t}. 
        \end{equation}
        Then $\bar u_1$ is a positive supersolution of \eqref{main_eq} for $t > \frac{\gamma}{\delta}$, $x \leq 2t - \frac{3}{2}\log t - Z_\delta(t)$, and $Z_\delta$ given by \eqref{Z_delta}.

[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2604.22461, 'Large deviation principles for stationary solutions and invariant measures of a class of S'] Let $\mathcal{P}_{W}(\sC_{-\infty} \times \W)$ denote the Borel probability space on $\sC_{-\infty} \times \W$ satisfying the marginal distribution on $\W$ is $\P \circ W^{-1}$. Let $S_{\Gamma} \subset \mathcal{P}_{W}(\sC_{-\infty} \times \W)$ denote the collection of $\cF_{t}$-adapted solution measures with the constraint $\Gamma$. If $S_{\Gamma} $ is a convex non-empty set, then the following are equivalent:
 \begin{itemize}
  \item [i)] Pathwise uniqueness holds for $\cF_{t}$-adapted martingale solutions. This means that if there are two $\cF_{t}$-adapted process $X^1_t$ and $X^2_t$ defined on the same probability space such that $\nu_{1}:=\P \circ (W, X^1)^{-1}$ and $\nu_{2}:=\P \circ (W, X^2)^{-1}$ both belong to $S_{\Gamma}$, then $X^1=X^2$, $\P$-a.s..
  \item [ii)] Joint uniqueness in law holds, and there exists a $\cF_{t}$-adapted strong solution. This means that $S_{\Gamma}$ contains at most one measure, denoted by $\nu$, and $\nu$ corresponds to an $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted process $X_{t}=\mathcal{G}(W)(t)$ such that the pair $(\omega, \mathcal{G}(W(\omega))$ satisfies the constraint $\Gamma$, where $\mathcal{G}: \W \rightarrow \sC_{-\infty}$ is a Borel measurable map.
 \end{itemize}

