[Lemma lem:limit and functional of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] If $\phi$ is a Banach-Mazur limit, then 
		\[\liminf_{n\to \infty}x_n\le \phi(\mathbf{x})\le\limsup_{n\to\infty}x_n\]
		for each $\mathbf{x}=(x_1,x_2,\cdots)\in \ell^\infty$. In particular, if the limit $\lim_{n\to\infty}x_n$ exists, then $\phi(\mathbf{x})= \lim_{n\to\infty}x_n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

