[Corollary 4 of arXiv:2609.01020, '2609.01020'] Assume that the C.I. subvariety $Y=\{f_1=\cdots =f_d=0\} 
\subset X=\CC^n$ has an isolated singular point at the origin $0\in Y$. 
Then we have 
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Eu}_Y(0)=\chi(M_{Y\cap H,0}) =1+(-1)^{n-d-1}\mu_{Y\cap H, 0},
\end{equation}
where $\mu_{Y\cap H}=\dim_{\CC} H^{n-d-1}(M_{Y\cap H,0}; \CC )$ is the Milnor number of 
the C.I. subvariety $Y\cap H \subset H$ of $H\simeq \CC^{n-1}$ at the origin 
$0\in Y\cap H$ (c.f. Hamm \cite{Ham71}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

