[Lemma 15 (One-dimensional PF-ODE $=$ monotone rearrangement) of arXiv:2607.25685, 'Mimicking diffusion processes with differential equations'] Let $d=1$ and let $(p_t)$ solve \eqref{eq:fp} with $\int_{-\infty}^{x}p_t$ finite, and set
$F_t(x):=\int_{-\infty}^xp_t$. Assume $p_t>0$ and $p_tv\in L^1_\loc$ with vanishing flux at
$-\infty$. Then
\begin{equation}
  \partial_tF_t(x)=-p_t(x)\,v(x,t),
\end{equation}
and consequently $t\mapsto F_t(Z_t)$ is constant along every absolutely continuous solution
of $\dot Z_t=v(Z_t,t)$. Hence, whenever the right-hand side is defined,
\begin{equation}
  Z(t,x)=F_t^{-1}\big(F_0(x)\big).
\end{equation}

[Cor cor-npoint of arXiv:2607.25567, 'Random Trees in Hyperbolic FPP'] There exists $\kappa > 0$ such that the following holds.
Let $a_1,\cdots, a_n, \xi$ be distinct points in ${\partial G}$ and $a, b$ adjacent interior vertices of ${\mathcal T}(a_1,\cdots, a_n, \xi)$, such that $d(a,b)\gg 0$. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mathbb{P}[d(a(\omega), b(\omega))\geq d(a,b) + N]\leq e^{-\kappa N}$,
\item  $\mathbb{P}[d(a(\omega), b(\omega))\leq d(a,b) - N]\leq e^{-\kappa N}$
\end{enumerate}

[Theorem thm:on-bank-truth-validity of arXiv:2608.20295, 'Physical-Support Confidence Sets for Highly Coherent Dictionaries'] Suppose the reported truth-level assertion $\widehat g$ is emitted only when
its predicate satisfies Equation~(equation eq:universal-truth-predicate of the paper), and
suppose the data-generating explanation $e_\star$ belongs to the bank.
Under Equation~(equation eq:on-bank-truth-retention of the paper),
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{e_\star\in\mathcal B}
    \mathbb P_{e_\star}
    \left\{
        \widehat g
        \text{ is reported and }
        q_{\widehat g}(e_\star)=0
    \right\}
    \le
    \alpha_{\mathcal B}.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] Let  $\tau_1,\tau_2,\dots,$ be i.i.d. random variables,  $\tau_j\simeq\mathrm{Beta}_{II}(\alpha,\alpha)$. Define $P_k=\prod_{j=1}^k \tau_j$ and $R_n=1+P_1+\dots+P_n$.
For fixed   $\theta>0$, we have:
\begin{equation} 
  \lim_{m\to\infty}  \sqrt{m}\, \EE[R_m^{-\theta}] =c
\end{equation}
for some $c\in(0,\infty)$.
Furthermore,
  for  $K>0$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{m\to\infty} \tfrac{\EE[(R_m+KP_m)^{-\theta}]}{\EE[R_m^{-\theta}]}=1.
\end{equation}

