[Lem secular of arXiv:2609.01034, 'The Multiple Timescales of Gradient Descent on~the~Edge~of~Stability: A~Perturbative~Deriv'] Let $\alpha, \beta \in \mathbb{R}$. The solutions $\varphi = \varphi(t_1)$ of the difference equation
    \begin{equation*}
        \Delta_{t_1} \varphi + 2 \varphi = \alpha + \beta (-1)^{t_1} 
    \end{equation*}
    are 
    \begin{equation*}
        \varphi = \frac{\alpha}{2} + a(-1)^{t_1} - \beta t_1 (-1)^{t_1} \, , \qquad a \in \mathbb{R} \, .
    \end{equation*}
    In particular, there exists a bounded solution if and only if $\beta = 0$.

