[Proposition 10 (H\"older estimates for the transformed coefficients) of arXiv:2608.29726, '\LARGE A Priori Estimates for Singular Fractional Stochastic Burgers Equations'] Assume the hypotheses of \Cref{prop:response,prop:zvonkin} and let
\(0<\rho\le\beta<1\).  Then the coefficients in
\eqref{eq:coefficients} satisfy
\begin{align}
  [a]_{C^\beta}
  &\lesssim_\Psi\norm{J-1}_{C^\beta},
  \\
  \norm{Q_0}_{C^\rho}
  &\lesssim_\Psi
  \norm{\ell}_{C^\rho}
  \bigl(1+\norm{J-1}_{C^\beta}\bigr),
  \\
  \norm R_{C^\rho}
  &\lesssim_\Psi\norm{\ell}_{L^\infty}\norm{\ell}_{C^\rho},
  \\
