[Proposition prop:first-counter-example of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] The functions
    \begin{align}
        f_1(\xi)\coloneqq \left(1-\frac{i\xi}{2}+\frac{\xi^2}{2}\right)^{-1},
        \qquad
        f_2(\xi)\coloneqq \left(1+\frac{i\xi}{2}+\frac{\xi^2}{2}\right)^{-1}
    \end{align}
    are characteristic functions on $\R$ satisfying (equation eq:defining-equation of the paper), but neither is of the form (equation eq:laplace of the paper). In particular, Problem~(problem-kac of the paper) is false as stated.

