[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2605.30560, 'Projected McKean--Vlasov Dynamics for Entropic Weak Optimal Transport'] Let $\mu\in \Pc_{1+\varepsilon}(\Xc)$ for some $\varepsilon>0$.
Then, for all $0\le \varepsilon'<\varepsilon$,
\[
\lim_{\delta\to0}
\sup_{\substack{
\gamma\in\Pi(\mu,\mu)\\
\E^\gamma[d_\Xc(X,X')]\le\delta
}}
\E^\gamma\big[d_\Xc(X,X')^{1 + \varepsilon'} \big]
=0.
\]

[Proposition P:ETnLB of arXiv:2604.08129, 'Polarity of points for Gaussian random fields in critical dimension'] Suppose $\gamma d \le 1$. Let $K_0$ be defined by (equation D:K0 of the paper).
Then there exists a constant $C_2 > 0$ and $\delta_0 \in (0, 1)$ small such that for all $\varepsilon \in (0, \delta_0)$ and $n = 2^p$ satisfying $n \le K_0 f(\varepsilon)$,
\begin{align}
{\mathbb E}[T_\varepsilon^n] \ge (C_2 n\varepsilon^d f(\varepsilon))^n.
\end{align}

