[Lemma LEM: CL-est of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that 
\begin{align}
Z_{x_0,\theta}=\mathcal{I}(1) \ge c e^{-cL},
\end{align}

\noindent
uniformly in $x_0\in \mathbb{T}_{L^2}$ and $\theta \in  [0,2\pi]$, where $\mathcal{I}(1)$ is as defined in (equation Idef of the paper).

