[Lem 6. lem: aging, convergence of traps for random electrical networks of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Under Assumption (1. assum: aging, random version of the paper), it holds that 
  \begin{equation} 
    \Bigl( V_{n}, a_{n}^{-1}R_{n}, \rho_{n}, b_{n} \mu^{\#}_{n}, \mathsf{P}_{n}\bigl( (c_{n}^{-1}\nu_{n}, \tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{n}^{\nu_{n}}) \in \cdot \bigr) \Bigr)
    \xrightarrow{\mathrm{d}}
    \Bigl( F, R, \rho, \mu, \mathsf{P}\bigl( (\nu, \mathcal{L}^{\nu}) \in \cdot \bigr) \Bigr)
  \end{equation}
