[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $G$ be as in \eqref{eq:functG} and $h:\R \rightarrow \R$ differentiable function. Then, we have
    \begin{displaymath}
        \E \big[ h(\lambda_{t}) \big] -  h(\lambda_{0})  =\int_{0}^{t} \E \Big(  \lambda_{s} \big[ h(\lambda_{s} + DG(s,X_{s})) - h (\lambda_{s}) - h'(\lambda_{s})DG(s,X_{s}) \big]  \Big)   \dd s
    \end{displaymath}

