[Theorem thm:Z-wellposed of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] Let Assumptions (ass:LR of the paper), (ass:diff2 of the paper) and~(ass:SC of the paper) hold, let $0 \leq s \leq T$ and $r \in [0,T]$, and let $\mathcal{Z}^{a}(t,s;r)v$ denote the solution of (equation eq:second-var of the paper)--(equation eq:Z-initial-cond of the paper) in the direction $a \in U$. Then for every $v \in H$ and every $a \in U$ this solution exists, is unique in $L^2(\Omega; C([\max(s,r),T]; H))$, and satisfies
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sup_{\max(s,r) \leq \tau \leq t} \norm{\mathcal{Z}^{a}(\tau, s; r)v}_H^2\Bigr] \;\leq\; C\,\lVert v \rVert_H^2\,\lVert a \rVert_U^2 ,
\end{equation}
the constant depending on $T, r, s$ and on the constants of \textup{(SC1)}--\textup{(SC3)}. The directions assemble, $\mathcal{Z}(t,s;r)v = (a \mapsto \mathcal{Z}^{a}(t,s;r)v)$ lying in $L^2(\Omega; C([\max(s,r),T]; L_2(U,H)))$ with
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sup_{\max(s,r) \leq \tau \leq t} \norm{\mathcal{Z}(\tau,s;r)v}_{L_2(U,H)}^2\Bigr] \;\leq\; C\,\lVert v \rVert_H^2 ,
\end{equation}
independently of the basis of $U$, and $(v,a) \mapsto \mathcal{Z}^{a}(t,s;r)v$ is bilinear. In the $r < s$ branch of (equation eq:Z-initial-cond of the paper) this holds for every $r$; in the $s \leq r$ branch, for every $r$ in Regime~A, where $\mathcal{B}'_u$ extends to $H$, and for almost every $r > s$ in Regime~B, where it acts only on $V$ (Remark~(rem:SC-raised-two-regimes of the paper)).

