body:
[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2603.25615, 'Fourier dimension of Mandelbrot cascades on planar curves'] Let $\beta<\widetilde{\tau}(2)$. Then, almost surely, 
    \begin{equation} 
|\widehat{\nu_{n+1}}(\xi)-\widehat{\nu_n}(\xi)|\lesssim_\beta b^{-n\beta/2}
\end{equation}
holds for all $n\in\N$ and all $\xi\in\R^d$, $|\xi|_\infty\le b^{n+1}$.  Here, the implicit constant is random, but independent of $n$ and $\xi$.

