[Lemma l:local_smoothing_iteration_velocity of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $Q=Q_{\varrho}(t_0,x_0)$ be a parabolic cylinder of side $\varrho\in (0,1]$ and center $(t_0,x_0)\in {\mathbb R}\times {\mathbb R}^d$. 
Suppose that (equation eq:parabolicity_localized_SMR of the paper) and (equation eq:smoothness_coefficients_localized_SMR of the paper) hold.
Fix $r\in (1,\infty)$, $p\in (2,\infty)$ and $\eta\in (0,1)$. Then for all $q_0\in [2,\infty)$ and $q_1\in (q_0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation}

q_1-q_0\leq 1/(dp),
\end{equation}
and all local solutions $(v,\pi,(\widetilde{\pi}_n)_n)$ to the stochastic Stokes system (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_xi_linear of the paper) in $Q$ for which 
\begin{align}

F,\, \|(G_n)_n\|_{\ell^2} &\in L^r_\mathscr{P}(\Omega;L^{p}(I;L^{q_1}(B))),\\

v&\in L^r(\Omega;L^{2}(I;H^{1,q_0}(B)))\cap L^r(\Omega;C(\overline{I};L^{q_0}(B))),\\

\pi&\in L^r(\Omega;L^{2}(I;L^{q_0}(B))),\\

(\widetilde{\pi}_n)_n&\in L^r(\Omega;L^{2}(I;H^{1,q_0}(B;\ell^2))),
\end{align}
one has 
\begin{equation}

v\in L^r(\Omega;L^{p}(\eta  I;H^{1,q_1}(\eta B)))\cap L^r(\Omega;C(\eta\overline{I};B^{1-2/p}_{q_1,p}(\eta B))),
\end{equation} 
with a corresponding estimate depending only on the norms of $F$, $\|(G_n)_n\|_{\ell^2}$, $v$, $\pi$ and $(\widetilde{\pi}_n)_n$ appearing in (equation eq:local_smoothing_iteration_velocity1 of the paper)-(equation eq:local_smoothing_iteration_velocity4 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor: equivalent asymptotique d lambda fois caractère à une certaine puissance r fini pour les caractères suffisamment de points fixes of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $r\geq 0$. Let $c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $. For each $n\geq 1$, let $\sigma_n\in {\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n$. Let $(t_n)$ be a sequence of positive real numbers such that $t_n = \frac{(\ln n)+c +o(1)}{\ln(n/f_1(\sigma_n))}$.
Assume that $f_1(\sigma_n)/\sqrt{n}\to \infty$. Then as $n\to \infty$, uniformly over all $\lambda \vdash n$ such that $\lambda_1 = n-r$, we have
\begin{equation}
    d_\lambda \chi^{\lambda}(\sigma_n)^{t_n}\to \frac{e^{-rc}}{r!}d_{\lambda^*},
\end{equation}
where $\lambda^* = (\lambda_2, \lambda_3, \ldots) \vdash r$ is the diagram $\lambda$ minus its first row. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

