[Theorem thm:malliavindersig of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Let $X$ be an Itô process defined by (equation eq:ito_proc_def of the paper). Assume that $a^{\sigX[]}_\cdot := (\sigX[\cdot] \otimes a^{i}_\cdot)_{i=0, 1, \ldots, d}$ satisfies  Assumption~(assump:Strato_reg_assump of the paper) elementwise, that is, coordinatewise with respect to each ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}} \in V$.
    Then, $\sigX[] \in \mathbb{L}^{1,2}$ elementwise and   for $\mathbb{P} \otimes ds \otimes dt\text{-almost every } (\omega, s, t) \in \Omega \times [0,T]^2$ with $s\leq t$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{D}_s \sigX = \sigX[s] \otimes A_s \otimes \sigX[s, t]
        + \int_s^t \sigX[u] \otimes \big(\mathbf{D}_s A_u \circ d\widehat{W}_u\big) \otimes \sigX[u, t],
    \end{equation}
    or, in coordinate form, for $i = 1, \ldots, d$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{D}_s^i \sigX[t]
        = \sigX[s] \otimes a_s^i \otimes \sigX[s, t]
        + \sum_{k=0}^d \int_s^t 
        \big(\sigX[u] \otimes \mathbf{D}_s^i a_u^k \otimes \sigX[u, t]\big) \circ d\widehat{W}_u^k.
    \end{equation}

[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2609.01166, 'Nonparametric inference for density-dependent McKean--Vlasov diffusions'] Under assumptions~\ref{ass:potential} and~\ref{ass:coefficient}, every candidate density satisfies
\begin{equation}
 |a_\xi-a_0| \leq 
 C_{d,K,V}
 \norm{\pi_\xi-\pi_0}_{L^1(\R^d)}^{2/(d+2)} 
 \leq 2^{1/(d+2)}C_{d,K,V}
 \KL(\pi_0\Vert\pi_\xi)^{1/(d+2)}
\end{equation}
with some constant 
\(C_{d,K,V}=C(d,K,V)>0\).
Thus, for every 
\(I=[r_-,r_+]\Subset(0,a_0)\), 
setting \(\eta_I=(a_0-r_+)/2\), there exists \(\varepsilon_{I,K,V,a_0}>0\) such that the inequality 
\(\KL(\pi_0\Vert\pi_\xi)
\leq\varepsilon_{I,K,V,a_0}\) 
implies \(a_\xi \ge r_+ + \eta_I\).

