[Proposition prop:5.3 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] For every $q\in (0,1)$ it holds in the limit $k\to\infty$ that
\begin{align*}
P_k(q)=\frac{q^{\binom{k+1}2}}{(q;q)_\infty}\left(1+O(q^k)\right) \quad \text{and} \quad
P_k(t;q)=\frac{q^{\binom k2}}{(q;q)_\infty}e^{t(1-q^{-k})}\left(1+O(q^k)\right).
\end{align*}

