[Theorem 2dsubcriticalSHE of arXiv:2511.08479, '\Large From disordered systems to the Critical 2D Stochastic Heat Flow'] Let $u^\varepsilon(t, x)$ be the solution of the mollified 2D SHE  (equation eq:mollSHE of the paper) with disorder strength
\begin{equation}
\beta_\varepsilon :=(\hat\beta +o(1))\sqrt{\frac{2\pi}{\log\frac{1}{\varepsilon}}}.
\end{equation}
Then for every $(t, x)\in (0, \infty)\times \mathbb{R}^2$, we have
 \begin{equation} 
	u^\varepsilon(t, x) \xrightarrow[\,N\to\infty\,]{dist}
	\begin{cases}
	\exp\big( \sigma_{\hat\beta} \, {\ensuremath{\mathcal N}} -
	\frac{1}{2} \sigma_{\hat\beta}^2
	\,\big)
	& \text{if } \hat \beta < 1 \\
	0 & \text{if } \hat\beta \ge 1
	\end{cases} \,.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

