and we need only bound the probability that $\sum_{t=i}^{i+r-1}\I{X_{t} \leq X_{t-1}\text{, }L_t>0} \le  \frac{\sqrt{C}}{15\sqrt{2}}$.\par
Since $|E(H_{t-1})| \le |E(H_{i-1})| +\sum_{s=i-1}^{t-1} d_s(v_s)$ the hypotheses imply that for 
all $t$ with $i\leq t \le i+r-1$, $|E(H_{t-1})|+X_{t-1} \le \frac{m}{10^5 }$.
