[Definition ping of arXiv:2603.17861, 'Gaussian concentration, integral probability metrics, and coupling functionals\\ for infin'] Let $\mu\in\mathscr{M}_\tau^1(\Omega)$ and let $C>0$. We say that $\mu$ satisfies the
\emph{thermodynamic Gaussian concentration bound with constant $C$} if for all $f\in\Delta_1(\Omega)$ the pressure $p(f|\mu)$ defined in (equation def-pressure of the paper) exists and satisfies the inequality
\begin{equation}
p(f-\mu(f)|\mu) \leq \scaleto{\frac{C}{2}}{18pt}\|\delta f\|_1^2\,.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 22 (Fixed-particle compact resolvent) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] For every fixed $(N,\beta)$, the nonnegative self-adjoint operator associated with the closed Dirichlet form $(\cE_{N,\beta},\mathsf D_{N,\beta})$ on $L^2(\mathbb P_{N,\beta})$ has compact resolvent, and its kernel consists only of constants.  Hence, $\mathbb P_{N,\beta}$ has a positive fixed-$(N,\beta)$ Poincar\'e gap.

Moreover, for every fixed $N$ and every compact interval $I\Subset(0,\infty)$,
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{\beta\in I}C_P(\mathbb P_{N,\beta})<\infty.
\end{equation}

