body:
[Definition def:weak_rec_grad of arXiv:2608.07042, 'Limit Points of Reflow with Minibatch Optimal Transport'] Let $\gamma\in\Gamma(\mu_0,\mu_1)$ and $\mu_t$ be defined by (equation eq:def_mu_t of the paper) and denote by $v_t^p=\argmin_{w_t\in \mathrm{T}_{\mu_t}}\mathcal L(w_t|\gamma)$ the solution of the flow matching loss (equation eq:flow_matching_loss of the paper) with gradient constraint.
Then, we define the set of weak rectified couplings with gradient constraint $\mathcal R_p(\gamma)$ as the set of all transport plans $\tilde \gamma$ given by
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{R}^d\times \mathbb{R}^d} \psi(x,y)  \mathrm{d}\tilde\gamma=  \int \psi(\lambda(0),\lambda(1)) \mathrm{d}\Lambda(\lambda),\quad\text{for all }\psi\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}^d),
\end{equation}
where $\Lambda$ fulfills (equation eq:Lambda1 of the paper) and (equation eq:Lambda2 of the paper) with respect to $v_t^p$.

[Theorem thrm:mix of arXiv:2511.01058, 'Limit profiles and cutoff for the Burnside process on Sylow double cosets'] Suppose \(p=p_m\) is a diverging sequence of prime numbers, and that \(k=k_m\) is a sequence of positive integers with \(k_m < p_m\) for all \(m\). Let \(P\) be the transition kernel for the Sylow--Burnside process on \(S_{pk}\) and let \(d(t)\) be as in equation (equation eq:dt of the paper).
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item If \(k_m \equiv k\) is eventually constant, then for all \(c \ge 0\),
              \begin{equation}
                  d(cp)\rightarrow 1-(1-e^{-c})^k.
              \end{equation}
        \item If \(k_m \to \infty\), then for all \(c \in \mathbb{R}\),
              \begin{equation}
                  d(p\log k + cp)  \to 1-\exp({-e^{-c}}). 
              \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition e:QalphaY of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting and $Y=(N,\Lambda)$. The generator of  $Y$ is given by

\begin{equation} 
  \begin{split}
    Q^\alpha f(n, \lambda)
    =& -\lambda f(n, \lambda) + \alpha(\beta-\lambda)f_\lambda (n, \lambda)\\
    &+\lambda \int\mathds{1}_{\{u < A-\lambda\}} f(n+1,u+\lambda) \,dG_{\ell}(n+1, u)\\
    &+\lambda f(0,{\lambda^o}) \bar{G}_{\ell}(n+1, (A-\lambda) \textrm{-}),
  \end{split}

\end{equation}
  where  $G_{\ell}(n, \cdot)$ is the distribution function defined in (equation e:Gell of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

