[Lemma lem:temporal of arXiv:2607.25694, 'Parameter Estimation of the Stochastic Allen--Cahn Equation via variations.'] Let \(G\) denote the heat kernel on \(\mathbb{R}\). For every \(t\in[0,T]\), \(x\in \mathbb{R}\), and \(h>0\), define
\begin{equation}
B_{t,x}(h):=\int_{\mathbb{R}}\left(\int_{0}^{t}\bigl|G_{t+h-s}(x-y)-G_{t-s}(x-y)\bigr|^{\beta}ds\right)^{\frac{1}{\beta}}dy\,\leq C_\beta h^{\frac{1}{\beta}}
\end{equation}
for all \(\beta\in(\frac{4}{3},2)\), with \(C_{\beta}>0\). Moreover, for the periodic heat kernel \(p\), we have for all \(t\in[0,T]\), \(x\in\mathbb{T}\), and \(h>0\) that
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{T}}\left(\int_{0}^{t}\bigl|p_{t+h-s}(x-y)-p_{t-s}(x-y)\bigr|^{\beta}ds\right)^{\frac{1}{\beta}}dy \leq B_{t,x}(h).
\end{equation}
Additionally, for the periodic heat kernel \(p\), we have for all \(t\in[0,T]\), \(x\in\mathbb{T}\), and \(h>0\) (small enough)
\begin{equation}
C_{t,x}(h):=\int_{t}^{t+h}\int_{\mathbb{T}}\left|p_{t+h-s}(x-y)\right|^{\beta}dy\,ds\leq C_{\beta}h^{\frac{3}{2}-\frac{\beta}{2}}
\end{equation}
for all \(\beta\in(0,3)\), with \(C_{\beta}>0\).

