[Lemma 17 (Exponential moment under the product path law) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under the assumptions of Proposition~\ref{prop:subgaussian}, let
$\bar X_1,\ldots,\bar X_N$ be independent nonlinear processes solving
\eqref{eq:nonlinear-sde}.  There are $\eta_0,C,L_0>0$, independent of
$N,s,t$, such that, for $0\le s\le t$,
\begin{equation}
  \E\exp\left\{
    \eta_0\int_s^t\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N\|\bar X_i(u)\|^2\,du
  \right\}
  \le Ce^{L_0(t-s)}.
\end{equation}

