where we use the fact that $\|w[t]\|$ is continuous in $t$ up to the existing time, which follows from the standard fixed point argument. By Lemma~(le:wh_bound of the paper), if $\varepsilon_0 \leq 1$ is small enough, on the event $\mathfrak{A} \cap ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:dc3c6b8e6ba159dfbb8ba7e86d0752fa95924316b5fdb2759415571f8885633d","revision_digest":"sha256:a0682033ce4bbb25d51a4975da7c8ea53039c2b00a3fe7e4250bc0dd092dcdcb","source_id":"arxiv:2411.03482","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

