[Proposition prop:localized-to-global-comparison of arXiv:2608.22910, 'A Commutator Framework for Selective Spectral Alignment in Deep Neural Networks'] At a fixed time, let \(A_\ell(x)\) be symmetric and square-integrable,
possibly independent of \(x\), and set
\begin{align*}
\mathcal E_{A,\ell}^{(k)}
&:=
\int\|\Pi_\ell^{(k)}A_\ell
\Pi_\ell^{(k),\perp}\|_F^2\,\, \mathrm{d}\mu,\qquad \mathcal C_{A,\ell}
:=
\int\|[A_\ell,P_\ell]\|_F^2\,\, \mathrm{d}\mu,
\end{align*}
where the integrals are omitted when \(A_\ell\) is deterministic. If
\(n=m_{\ell+1}\) and
\(\underline\gamma_\ell:=\min_{1\leq k<n}\gamma_\ell^{(k)}>0\), then
\begin{equation}
2\underline\gamma_\ell^2
\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}\mathcal E_{A,\ell}^{(k)}
\leq
\mathcal C_{A,\ell}
\leq
2\|P_\ell\|_{\mathrm{op}}^2
\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}\mathcal E_{A,\ell}^{(k)}.
\end{equation}

