[Lemma 7 (Comparison of low-energy cutoff masses) of arXiv:2609.01436, '2609.01436'] If $F,G\in\mathcal B_1^+([0,\infty))$ satisfy \(N(F)=N(G)\), then
\begin{equation}
 \abs{N_{0,2}(F,\varepsilon)-N_{0,2}(G,\varepsilon)}
 \leq\frac2\varepsilon\norm{F-G}_1^\circ.
\end{equation}

