[Lemma lem-pathinteraction of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] Suppose that Assumption (V) holds. Then there is a $C\in(0,\infty)$ (only depending on $d$, $v$ or $\beta$) such that, for any box $W$ of diameter $R\in\mathbb{N}$ that is contained in the box $\Lambda\subset \mathbb{R}^d$, and for any $k\in\mathbb{N}$ that is sufficiently large (depending on $R$),
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\big[{\operatorname e }^{-\Phi_{\Lambda,\Lambda}}\big]\leq {\operatorname e }^{-Ck^{3/2}R/\sqrt{|W|}},\qquad  x_1,\dots,x_k\in W,
\end{equation}
where $\mathbb{E}=\bigotimes_{i=1}^k \mathbb{P}_{x_i}$ is with respect to $k$ independent Brownian motions with time interval $[0,\beta]$, starting from $x_1,\dots,x_k\in W$ and having any of the three boundary conditions in $ \Lambda$, and $\Phi_{\Lambda,\Lambda}$ is the interaction between all the $k$ motions.

