[Definition def:sol of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Fix $s\in (0,d/2)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1)$. An $\dot{H}^{-s}$-valued, probabilistically weak solution to (equation eq:KK of the paper) is a tuple $(\Omega,\mathcal{A},(\mathcal{F}_t)_t,\mathbb{P},W^\mathcal{K},M)$, where $(\Omega,\mathcal{A},(\mathcal{F}_t)_t,\mathbb{P})$ is a filtered probability space (satisfying the standard assumption), $W^\mathcal{K}$ is a $(\mathcal{F}_t)_t$-adapted Wiener process with covariance function $Q$ (given in (equation eq:Q_spectrum of the paper)), and $M$ is an $\dot{H}^{-s}_{\div}$-valued, $(\mathcal{F}_t)_t$-progressively measurable process $M$ such that $M\in L^2_t(\dot{H}^{-s}_{\div})\cap C_t(H^{-s-2}_{\div})$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.\ and
    \begin{align}
        M_t = M_0 -\int_0^t B[M_r] \,\mathrm{d} W^\mathcal{K}_r +\int_0^t \frac{c_0}{2}\DeltaM_r \,\mathrm{d} r,\quad \forall t\in[0,T],
    \end{align}
    where the equality makes sense in $H^{-s-2}_{\div}$ thanks to (cor:stoch_int_bd of the paper).

