body:
[Thm main-general of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Fix $d\ge 2$. Suppose Assumption~(assump:uniform-mixing-time of the paper) holds. There exists $p_0(d)<1$ such that for all $p>p_0$ and all $\beta > \beta_0$, if $X_t$ is continuous-time Glauber dynamics on $\mathbb T^d_n = (\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z)^d$, with probability $1-o(1)$, $x_0 \sim \bigotimes_{\mathbb T_n^d}\text{Rad}(p)$ is such that 
    \begin{align*}
        \|\mathbb P_{x_0} (X_t \in \cdot) - \pi^+_{\mathbb T^d_n}\|_{{\textsc{tv}}} \le n^{-10} \qquad \text{ for all $t\in [n^{o(1)}, e^{ \Omega(n^{d-1})}]$}\,.
    \end{align*}
    If $X_t$ is the infinite volume Glauber dynamics on $\mathbb Z^d$, with probability going to $1$ as $R\to\infty$, $x_0\sim \bigotimes _{\mathbb Z^d} \text{Rad}(p)$ is such that for $\Lambda_R = \{-\frac{R}{2},...,\frac{R}{2}\}^2$, once $t \ge R$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \|\mathbb P_{x_0}(X_t(\Lambda_R)\in \cdot) - \pi^+_{\mathbb Z^d}(\sigma(\Lambda_R)\in \cdot)\|_{{\textsc{tv}}} \le \exp( - \Omega((\log t)^{10}))\,.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2605.02713, '2605.02713'] Let $q \in \N \backslash \{1 \}$ and ${r \in \left\{ 1 , \ldots , q-1 \right\}}$. Define
	\begin{align*}
		s(n,r):= \sum_{i,j,k,l=1}^n     \alpha_n^{r|i-j|}   \alpha_n^{r|k-l|}   \alpha_n^{(q-r)|i-k|}   \alpha_n^{(q-r)|j-l|}  .
	\end{align*}
	Then it holds $\displaystyle \max_{r \in \left\{ 1 , \ldots , q-1 \right\}} s(n,r) = s(n,1) = s(n,q-1) $.

