[Lemma lem:local_step_concentration of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] For $\alpha \in (0,\frac{1}{2})$ there is some $c > 0$ such that, for all $e \in \binom{[n]}{2}$ with $v \in e$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[ | \mathsf{N}^{\rho \to v}_G(X,e) - \mathsf{d}_\rho p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} | > n^{\mathsf{v} - 2.5 + \alpha} \mright]
    \leq \Exp{- c n^{2\alpha}}.
\end{equation}

