body:
[Lemma lm:Start of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] Under the assumptions~((a:center of the paper))--((a:growth of the paper)) above, for the normalised variables~$\eta_{a;n}$, defined by~(equation eq:eta-family of the paper), the following estimate holds. There exists $\rho_0 > 0$, such that for any $n\ge n_0$, \emr{where $n_0$ is given by Lemma~(l:var-lower of the paper)}, and any~$a$ the value $N_{\rho_0} (\eta_{a;n})$ is well-defined and satisfies
    \begin{equation*}
        N_{\rho_0} (\eta_{a;n}) < 3 \overline{C}^{\textcolor{black}{2+{\varepsilon}}} \quad \text{and} \quad \rho_0^{\textcolor{black}{2+{\varepsilon}}} N_{\rho_0} (\eta_{a;n}) < \frac{1}{100},
    \end{equation*}
    where $\overline{C}$ is the constant defined in Corollary~(c.3 of the paper).

    Moreover, the choice of $\rho_0$ depends only on the constants under the assumptions~((a:center of the paper))--((a:growth of the paper)).

