[Lem h-eternal of arXiv:2604.12963, 'Shocks, instability, and the twenty networks\\ of infinite geodesics in the Directed Lands'] For any $\omega\in\Omega_0$, $\theta\in\Theta^\omega$, and $x_0,s_0\in\mathbb{R}$, $h^\theta_{(x_0,s_0)}$ is an eternal solution: for any $x$ and $t>s$ in $\mathbb{R}$,
