[Lemma LemmaGaussianGroundStateConvolution of arXiv:2608.11178, 'A submartingale for the probability of avoiding the origin in one-point interaction ground'] For every \(t>0\) and \(x\in\mathbb R^d\setminus\{0\}\), with
\(d\in\{2,3\}\), the Gaussian convolution of the ground-state
eigenfunction is given by
\begin{align}
(g_t*\psi_\gamma)(x)
=
\frac{
\sqrt{2\lambda_\gamma}
}{
\pi^{(d-1)/2}|x|^{d/2-1}
}
e^{\lambda_\gamma t}
K_{d/2-1}\!\left(
\sqrt{2\lambda_\gamma}\,|x|,
\lambda_\gamma t
\right). \nonumber
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop dissiBanach of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Let $f:{\rm Dom}(f)\subseteq \mathcal{K}{\rightarrow}\mathcal{K}$. $f$ is dissipative if and only if, for every $x,y\in {\rm Dom}(f)$ there exists $z^*\in\partial{\left\|x-y\right\|}$ such that
\begin{equation}
\dscal{f(x)-f(y)}{z^*}{\mathcal{K}}\leq 0.
\end{equation}
If $\mathcal{K}$ is a Hilbert space (equation disban of the paper) reads as
\begin{equation*}
\scal{f(x)-f(y)}{x-y}_{\mathcal{K}}\leq 0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 71 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Assume $\omega$ is such that $\cC_1(p_0) \subseteq \cC_1(p_1)$. Denote by $\nu_1$ and $\nu_2$ the laws of $\ClCp{1}{p_0}$ and $\cT_{p_1 \mid p_0}$, respectively. Then
    \begin{equation} 
        \Vert \nu_1 - \nu_2\Vert_{\mathrm{TV}} \leq n^4 e^{-\beta(p_1 - p_0)},
    \end{equation}
    where $\Vert \cdot \Vert_{\mathrm{TV}}$ is the total variation norm. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm exponentialconvergence of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] Let us suppose that (A4 of the paper),(A7 of the paper)--(A12 of the paper) hold true. Furthermore, suppose that the constants given in the hypotheses satisfy
\begin{align}
\kappa \coloneqq m_x + m_\lambda - 2L_\mu - \sigma_{\lambda}C_{Q}> 0,
\end{align}
and consider $\mu_{\cdot}$ as in (equation misurasol of the paper). Then there exists a unique invariant probability measure $\mu_\infty \in {\mathscr{P}}_{2}({\mathscr Y})$ such that for every initial condition $(Y(0),\Lambda(0))\in L^{2}(\Omega,{\mathscr Y})$ of (equation eq:limitMV_detailed of the paper),
\begin{align}
{\mathcal W}_{2}(\mu(t), \mu_\infty)
\le
e^{-\kappa t} {\mathcal W}_{2}(\mu_0,\mu_\infty),
\end{align}
where $\mu_{0}={\mathcal L}((Y(0),\Lambda(0)))$ is the law of $(Y(0),\Lambda(0))$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

