[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2609.01826, 'An extension theory for fully fractional Schr\"odinger equations with memory'] Let $0<s<1, t>0$, and $z>0$. Then the following oscillatory identity holds:
\begin{equation}
\int_0^t
\frac{e^{i \frac{z^2}{4\sigma}}}{(t-\sigma)^{1-s}\sigma^{1+s}}\,d\sigma =
4^s\,\G(s)\,e^{i\frac{\pi s}{2}}\,t^{s-1}\,z^{-2s}
e^{i \frac{z^2}{4t}}.
\end{equation}

