[Lem l:lclt.fourier of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $\beta_0>0$ such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$ and $N \ge e^{\frac{11}{5}\beta}$ and $|H|\leq 2-\beta^{-1}\delta$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{k\in \mathbb Z} \Big| D_{N,H}^{1/2}  P_{N,H}(h(S_{N,H}) = k)  - e^{ - \frac{1}{2D_{N,H}} (k - M_{N,H})^2}\Big| \le C(\delta) e^{-\beta/100} \,, 
    \end{align*}
    for a constant $C(\delta)$ only depending on $\delta$.

