body:
[Prop sign-permute of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $(\xi_k)_{k\geq1}$ be a sequence of i.i.d. symmetric signs. Let $(X_k)_{k\geq1}$ be any sequence of random variables independent of $(\xi_k)_{k\geq 1}$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{k=1}^\infty \mathbb E[X_k^2] <\infty.
    \end{equation}
    Then, 
    \begin{equation}
        S = \lim_{N\to\infty}\sum_{k=1}^N\xi_kX_k
    \end{equation}
    exists as a limit in $L^2(\mathbb P)$, and also
    \begin{equation}
        S = \lim_{N\to\infty}\sum_{k=1}^N\xi_{\pi(k)}X_{\pi(k)}
    \end{equation}
    for any (random) permutation $\pi:\mathbb N\to\mathbb N$ independent of the signs $(\xi_k)_{k\geq1}$, that may possibly depend on the values of $(X_k)_{k\geq1}$.

