[Lemma lem:Luk.Wishart.Lemma.2.5 of arXiv:2606.04859, 'Stein's method for the Wishart distribution'] Let $\alpha > 3d-3$, $t\geq 0$, and $k\in \mathbb{N}$. Suppose that $h\in C^{kd}(\mathcal{S}_{++}^d)$, and that for every differential monomial $\overline{
abla}$ of order at most $kd$ in the entries of $
abla_{\!X}$, including the order-zero monomial, there exist constants $C_{\overline{
abla}}, N_{\overline{
abla}}\geq 0$ such that
 egin{equation}
|\overline{
abla} h(X)| \leq C_{\overline{
abla}} (1 + \|X\|_F^{N_{\overline{
abla}}}), \qquad X\in \mathcal{S}_{++}^d.
\end{equation}
Then, for every $(i_1, j_1), \ldots, (i_k, j_k)\in [d]^2$ and $\Lambda\in \mathcal{S}_{++}^d$,
 egin{equation}
\left(\prod_{\ell=1}^k 
abla_{\Lambda, i_{\ell} j_{\ell}}ight) (\mathcal{Q}_t h)(\Lambda)
= e^{-2kt} \, \mathsf{E}\left[\left(\prod_{\ell=1}^k \mathcal{D}_{i_{\ell} j_{\ell}}ight) h(\mathfrak{Y}_{k,t})ight],
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{D} = 
abla_{\!X} \, \mathrm{adj}(I_d - 2
abla_{\!X})$, $\mathfrak{Y}_{k,t}\sim \mathcal{W}_d(\alpha + 2k, I_d, e^{-2t}\Lambda)$ and is defined in (equation eq:Wishart.Q.operator.def of the paper).

