Conditional on independent copies $V_1,\ldots,V_k$, the normalized sum
\[
 \frac{Z_1+\cdots+Z_k}{\sqrt k}
\]
is Gaussian with variance
\[
 \overline V_k:=\frac{V_1+\cdots+V_k}{k}.
\]
Therefore
\begin{equation}
 b_{p,k}
 =\frac1{\sqrt{2\pi}}\,
 \E\,\overline V_k^{-1/2}.
\end{equation}
The sample means decrease in convex order: $\overline V_{k+1}\cx \overline V_k$. Indeed, choose uniformly a $k$-element subset $I$ of $\{1,\ldots,k+1\}$, independently of the variables. The average $k^{-1}\sum_{i\in I}V_i$ has the same law as $\overline V_k$, and its conditional expectation ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:2bd2cf37f77040a6427958ad2543786497fd1b04fa513ef26ae28872b2383c35","revision_digest":"sha256:a8681523f58753b10080b175fb65ca9908b25330954086ab13d19c55ced6bf63","source_id":"arxiv:2605.11451","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

