body:
[Lemma lem:width_from_contour of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] For any tree $T$ of size $n$, if we let $C^{(T)}=(C^{(T)}_t:0\leq t \leq 2n-1)$ be its contour walk, $w(T)$ its width, then 
\begin{align*}
    \frac{L_{2n-1}(C^{(T)})}{2}\leq w(t) \leq  L_{2n-1}(C^{(T)}).
\end{align*}

[Definition def-weak-strong-uniqueness-infty of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] We say that
	$\mathcal{C}_0 \subset \mathbb{X}^\infty_{\alpha,\beta}$ is a weak-strong uniqueness class of (equation PDE-infty of the paper)  if for every control $g\in L^2_{loc}([0,\infty);H)$, the following holds:   for arbitrary two weak solutions $\theta_1,\theta_2$ of the skeleton equation (equation PDE-infty of the paper) in the sense of Definition (def-sol-infinity of the paper)  with the same initial data $\theta_1(0)=\theta_2(0)$ and the same control $ g $, we have $\theta_1=\theta_2$ in  $ \mathbb{X}_{\alpha,\beta}^\infty$ as long as $\theta_1\in\mathcal{C}_0$ and  $\theta_2$ satisfies the $ H^{\alpha-2\beta}$-energy inequality: for every $ t>0 $,
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{1}{2}\|\theta_2(t)\|_{H^{\alpha-2\beta}(\mathbb{T}^2)}^2+\int_0^t\|\theta_2(s)\|_{H^{2\alpha-2\beta}(\mathbb{T}^2)}^2 \,\mathrm{d}s \leqslant \frac{1}{2}\left\|\theta_2(0)\right\|_{H^{\alpha-2\beta}(\mathbb{T}^2)}^2+\int_0^t\langle\Lambda^{2\alpha-2\beta} \theta_2, g\rangle \,\mathrm{d}s.
	\end{equation}

