[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2608.22597, 'Scale-invariant Optimal Sampling for Rare-events Data with Sparse Models'] Under the constraints that $\Exp\{\varphi(\x)\}=1$ and a given $\rho$ at
  the same order of $e^{\alpha_{\rt}}$,
the A-optimal function that minimizes $\text{tr}(\V_{\rw(\cA)})$ is 
\begin{equation}

\varphi_{\mmse}^{\radp}(\x)=\frac{p(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\|\M_{(\cA)}^{-1}\dg_{(\cA)}(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\|}{
\Exp\left\{p(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\|\M_{(\cA)}^{-1}\dg_{(\cA)}(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\right\}}.
\end{equation}
The L-optimal function that minimizes $\text{tr}(\M_{\rw(\cA)})$ is 
\begin{equation}

\varphi_{\mvc}^{\radp}(\x)=\frac{p(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\|\dg_{(\cA)}(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\|}{
\Exp\left\{p(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\|\dg_{(\cA)}(\x;\btheta_{\rt})\right\}}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:asymptotic-LaCroix-coefficients of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] For every $g\in\frac12\mathbb Z_{\geq0}$ and
$0\leq i\leq\lfloor g\rfloor$, the following limit exists and is independent
of the approximating integer sequences in~(equation eq:map-edge-powers of the paper):
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \lim_{N\to\infty}
  N^{2-m-2g}4^{-E_N}
  \operatorname{Map}^{\mathrm{LC}}_{g,i}
  (K_{1,N},\ldots,K_{m,N})
  =
  2C_2^m
  \mathbf B_{m-1+i,\,2g-2i}^{\mathrm{conn}}
  \left[\frac{\mu_+\mathfrak c_2}{2}\boldsymbol k\right].
  }

\end{equation}
In particular, every fixed La Croix coefficient has an explicit finite
nonnegative Brownian integral formula.

[Lemma 31 (Rudin--Shapiro bounds) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] For every $N\geq1$ and $|z|=1$,
\begin{equation}

    \int_Y |P_N(y,z)|^2\,d\nu(y)=N,
    \qquad
    \sup_{y\in Y}|P_N(y,z)|\leq\sqrt{10N}.
\end{equation}

