[Lemma L:Second-der-X-W2W2 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the process $D_{r_1,r_2}^{W_2 W_2} X_t^{\varepsilon}$ be the solution of equation (equation E:Second-der-Y-W2-W2 of the paper). Then, for any $p \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t \ge r_1 \vee r_2,$ there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{E} \left[\left|D_{r_1,r_2}^{W_2 W_2} X_t^{\varepsilon}\right|^{2p} \right]  \le K \left[ \varepsilon^{2p} +\eta^{2p} + \varepsilon^{p}\eta^{p}\right] e^{-(2p)\alpha (t- r_1 \wedge r_2)}
+ K e^{-(2p)\alpha (t- r_1 \vee r_2)} e^{-(2p)\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (r_1 \vee r_2 - r_1 \wedge r_2)}.
\end{equation*}

