[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$ be resilient. Then for any $\delta<\delta_c(\lambda)$ there exists constants $C,c \in (0,\infty)$ such that, for any $t>0$ and $\hat{\lambda} \geq \lambda$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \bP_{\hat{\lambda},\delta} \left( t \leq \tau^o <\infty \right) \leq Ce^{-ct}
    \end{equation}
    where $\tau^o \coloneqq \inf \{ t >0 \colon \eta_t^o=\underline{0} \}$ is the time until extinction of the infection process.

