[Lemma lem:sig_bound of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t \in [0, T]}$ be a continuous semimartingale and let $\sigXhat[]$ denote its time-augmented signature. Then, for any word ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}} \in V\,$, there exists a constant $C_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}, T} \geq 0\,$, such that
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        \left|\sigXhat[s,t]^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}}\right| &\leq C_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}, T}\,\left(1 + \left|X_{s,t}\right|^{|{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}|_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}}} + \int_s^t|X_{s,r}|^{|{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}|_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}}}dr\right), \quad s \leq t \leq T\,, \\
        \left|\sigXhat[s,t]^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v0}}}}\right| &\leq C_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}, T}\left(1 + \int_s^t|X_{s,r}|^{|{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}|_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}}}dr\right), \quad s \leq t \leq T\,.
    \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}

[Lemma fractionleib of arXiv:2606.31155, 'The well-posedness of stochastic Korteweg--de Vries equations revisited'] Let $s\geq 0$, $u\in H^s_x$. We have 
		\begin{equation*}
			\| u(x) \Phi e_j\|_{l^2_j H^s_x} =\|u(x)k(x,y)\|_{L^2_y H^s_x}\lesssim \|u\|_{H^s_x}\|J^s_xk\|_{L_x^\infty L_y^2}.
		\end{equation*}

