[Lem finite-direction-renewal-bound of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] For every fixed $\beta\geqslant0$ and $\eta>0$, there are constants
$C_{\beta,\eta}<\infty$ and $\ell_0<\infty$ such that, for all
$\ell\geqslant\ell_0$ and all $t\geqslant0$,
\begin{align}
\E\sum_{v\in\mathcal{N}_t^{(\ell)}}e^{\beta \mathsf{p}_\ell(v)}
\leqslant
C_{\beta,\eta}
\exp\{(\gk_\theta(\beta)+\eta)t\}.

\end{align}
Here $\gf(0)=1$ and hence $\gk_\theta(0)=1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

