[Theorem thm:Main of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $d, m \in \mathbb{N}$ be fixed with $d, m \geqslant 2$. Consider a sequence $\{\mathbf{X}^{(n)}\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ of generalised Bernoulli--Laplace chains where the $n^{\mathrm{th}}$ chain has parameters $(d, m, n, \mu_n)$. Suppose that the Cheeger constant of the single ball transition matrix satisfies $\Phi_{\ast}^{(n)} = \Omega(1)$. Then, for any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, we have
    \begin{equation}

        \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{t^{(n)}_{\textup{mix}}(\varepsilon)}{mn t_{\textup{mix,\,single}}^{(n)}(1/\sqrt{n})} = 1,
    \end{equation}
    where $t_{\textup{mix,\,single}}^{(n)}(1/\sqrt{n})$ denotes the $(1/\sqrt{n})$-mixing time of the rate $1$ single ball chain. In particular, the sequence $\{\mathbf{X}^{(n)}\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ exhibits cutoff. Moreover, the cutoff window is of size $O(n)$. Further, if $\mu_n$ is symmetric for each $n \in \mathbb{N}$, then the equality in (equation eqn:mix of the paper) continues to hold under the assumption that $\Phi_{\ast}^{(n)} = \Omega(n^{\alpha-1})$ for some $\alpha > 0$, with a cutoff window of size $O(n/\gamma_n)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lmm Wc of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] For \(W_\circ(\cdot,\cdot)\) defined in (equation Wcirc of the paper), none of the optimizers of
\[

\inf_{{\boldsymbol f}=(f,1-f):\  G_{W_\circ,\mathbf 1_1}(\boldsymbol f)=1/4}
\left\{
\int_0^1
f(u)\log \frac{f(u)}{p}
+
(1-f(u))\log\frac{1-f(u)}{1-p}
du
\right\}
\]
is a constant function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

