\begin{equation*}
	\psi''(z)=m(m-1)\frac{(1+z)^{m-2}}{z}\ge 0\,,\quad z>0\,,\qquad \psi(1)=0\,,\qquad \psi'(1)=-\phi''(1)\,.
\end{equation*}
Hence $\psi'(z)\ge -\phi''(1)$ for $z\ge 1$ while $\psi'(z)\le -\phi''(1)$ for $z\le 1$. Integration then yields~\eqref{L20a}.

