body:
[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2607.23305, 'On extremes of a random walk with positive drift\\ over an intermediate regularly varying '] Let $\E\xi=-a<0$ and let the distribution $F$ of $\xi$ 
be intermediate regularly varying at infinity. Then
\begin{eqnarray*}
\P\{\theta>n\} &\sim& \E\theta\overline F(na)\quad\mbox{as }n\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray*}

